{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways","id":1427414,"title":"So changing ways?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-05T18:30:52-08:00","id":1427414,"title":"So changing ways?","content":"So I hear that paradox changed changing ways, and that there was a manuscript of the earlier version. What all did paradox change in it? Or is this an unfounded rumor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T20:12:21-08:00","id":1427419,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that they asked to add transphobic content to the book that the writer did not himself add. I've seen the writer's side of things, but not Onyx Path's. Or WW/Paradox for that matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T21:41:28-08:00","id":1427423,"title":"","content":"The original manuscript was never released to the public.<br /> <br /> However, it's also not an unfounded rumor as one of the authors and the developer have both confirmed that WW/Paradox demanded edits of the material.<br /> <br /> The author was the only one to point out specific changes publicly.<br /> <br /> AFAIK Onyx Path has never officially said anything about it, and WW/Paradox only gave a boilerplate response that they exercised their rights as IP owners under the license to request alterations to the text.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-05T21:48:34-08:00","id":1427424,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d be curious to see what the original was but I reckon that\u2019ll be one of those things you\u2019ll see on eBay in 20 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T02:36:02-08:00","id":1427441,"title":"","content":"What would be the transphobic content that is now in the book?<br /> I didn't read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T07:21:58-08:00","id":1427455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427424#post1427424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d be curious to see what the original was but I reckon that\u2019ll be one of those things you\u2019ll see on eBay in 20 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how we're ever going to see it.<br /> <br /> The drafts belong to the WoD IP owners. They're not valuable enough to possible make any money off of that's worth the risk of getting sued. Paradox has no reason to allow it to get out since it'd just make them look bad.<br /> <br /> If the IP changes hands a time or two, it's likely work documents like that are going to be lost in the digital ether.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427441#post1427441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be the transphobic content that is now in the book?</div> </div> </div> </div>The central issue (though there are many) is that the book assigns a vary modern very specific real-world cultural position to the Garou that doesn't make any sense for them to hold: Garou shouldn't transition because Gaia doesn't make mistakes.<br /> <br /> This is, of course, a very fundamentalist Abrahamic stance because divine infallibility is central to many hard-line conservative Abrahamic religious groups. The Garou don't have any sort of belief that everything Gaia does is perfect (she created the Trait... that didn't go so well, and she created the Fera and the Garou waged multiple genocidal war with their fellow shifters... so Gaia's not exactly coming out doing things perfectly here). There isn't some grand ineffable plan Gaia has created that everyone is following.<br /> <br /> There's also a very tiresome repetition of equating being trans with gender affirming surgery or HRT; the text makes it sound like a Garou is incapable of being trans without physical changes, and that such changes are impossible due to Garou physiology (in direct contradiction to established lore and other sections of the same book). It's esp. jarring because as best you can piece together from what Holden has said about his draft, they basically took what was supposed to be, &quot;the Garou are distrustful of using Weaver tools to transition, but they have found spiritual methods to affirm gender identity that are better if you can convince the spirits to do it,&quot; and changed it to, &quot;trying to transition as a Garou is horrible icky badness. Oh but some spirits can snap their fingers and do it for you if you do a quest for them.&quot;<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that this material has always been in the published version of the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T11:32:03-08:00","id":1427471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(she created the Trait... that didn't go so well,</div> </div> </div> </div>Gaia made the Triat? Is there any source for this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T12:39:36-08:00","id":1427479,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s a common Garou belief, however its disputed by other Changing Breeds such as the Ananasi and Bastet who claim that it was the other way around, the Triat creating Gaia.<br /> <br /> In my mind, it\u2019s a matter of perspective. Ultimately the forces of the universe embodied by the Triat are what allowed Gaia to form and within Gaia the forces of the Triat play out to ensure the continuation of life. If you\u2019re only interested in Earth and it\u2019s life then focusing upon Gaia as the ultimate spiritual being makes a certain amount of sense, although in the broader sense, it may not be entirely accurate.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though as with much of cosmology, paradigm and perspective will play a large role in your understanding of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T12:42:04-08:00","id":1427480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller's Handbook revised page 137</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Which Is Bigger, Gaia or the Triat?</b><br /> The answer to this question has been left deliberately vague. Some Storytellers prefer to interpret the cosmology such that the Triat is universal, whereas Gaia is limited to the immediate vicinity of Earth (both physical and spiritual). Others prefer the idea that Gaia is the Universe, and that the Triat are her wayward children \u2014 albeit children with the power to slay their mother, should it come to that.<br /> The Changing Breeds themselves don\u2019t know the answer to this question, although they have their own ideas, and often blatantly disagree. Therefore, don\u2019t worry aboutany \u201cbook-legal\u201d right or wrong answer to the question \u2014 your answer is the one that matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I vaguely remember some Garou Legends stating the Triat was created by Gaia. But I think it is left open to interpretation in any case...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T12:59:43-08:00","id":1427482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427480#post1427480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I vaguely remember some Garou Legends stating the Triat was created by Gaia. But I think it is left open to interpretation in any case...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes Garou tend to view Gaia as supreme above the Triat, while Bastet are noted for more often viewing Gaia as the Incarna of Earth and the Triat as cosmic in comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T13:01:10-08:00","id":1427483,"title":"","content":"Anyway, Changing Ways is the only OPP published book where I have seen writers explicitly disown their sections because of changes made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T13:55:10-08:00","id":1427491,"title":"","content":"I believe there's also a section which describes a caern where every female Garou is <b>required</b> to bear at least one metis. Consider the implications of this, in lack of consent/rape, horrific injury, and death in childbirth. Yeah, and the metis are used as shock troops, kinda like how BSDs do it. And other Garou are aware of this Litany-spurning sept, but not even the Black Furies have attacked it. I doubt that Holden wrote that section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 12-06-2020, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T00:26:51-08:00","id":1427528,"title":"","content":"The ret-con of Avatar storm and the Malady is also an added content.<br /> <br /> As we can now see, the Malady is a WW 5e stuff. Why almost cut the Umbra of from the gameplay is a concept I can't understand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427480#post1427480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I vaguely remember some Garou Legends stating the Triat was created by Gaia. But I think it is left open to interpretation in any case...</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the Hengeyokai idea the most (If I remember &amp; interpret it right): Gaia created the Triat, but with it she lost her power and started to die. As a last act she died-birthed herself anew.<br /> So Gaia II is not the Gaia I the creator, but a creation and not superior to Triat as Gaia I was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":562,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","user":"Lachdanan","date":". 12-07-2020, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T00:29:32-08:00","id":1427529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427491#post1427491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe there's also a section which describes a caern where every female Garou is <b>required</b> to bear at least one metis. Consider the implications of this, in lack of consent/rape, horrific injury, and death in childbirth. Yeah, and the metis are used as shock troops, kinda like how BSDs do it. And other Garou are aware of this Litany-spurning sept, but not even the Black Furies have attacked it. I doubt that Holden wrote that section.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, it gets MUCH worse. It isn't JUST one sept, it is -multiple- septs doing this and treating their metis solely as animals/shock troops. This after the start of the metis section goes to VERY detailed lengths to showcase how dangerous birthing just ONE metis is.<br /> <br /> Add in an NPC popping up randomly to explain tribes and just the general non-functionality of this plan... it is a mess. As in, even BSDs don't solely rely on metis-breeding to bolster their numbers. This in addition to the REALLY nasty implications in the lupus section.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T01:21:35-08:00","id":1427533,"title":"","content":"As the parts of the book is written from the perspective of the storytelling werewolves, let's just assume they were infected by Wyrm or mind-wiped by Nephandi...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T02:25:13-08:00","id":1427540,"title":"","content":"I mostly treat Changing Ways as &quot;Not appearing in my library.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T03:37:14-08:00","id":1427546,"title":"","content":"The lore content of the game is generally not something I need for my games. However the book does have a lot of decent mechanical stuff: rules for what it takes to do body modification on a Garou, the custom pack tactics, the new rites and Gifts. The new Metis deformities are... hit or miss thematically, but the mechanics tend to be fine. The section on coming up with new rites and modifying existing ones is fairy sparse on the mechanical side of things (though I can't really blame them, as the official Rites are a mechanical nightmare of inconsistency) but it's still a solid part of the book.<br /> <br /> So it gets a solid, &quot;mechanics from CW20 assume yes, lore from CW20 assume no,&quot; for my games.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T03:48:13-08:00","id":1427547,"title":"","content":"For me, and this is truly just because I was waiting on this book to replace Way of the Wolf and Guardians of the Caerns, it had some good parts in it. The last two chapters are solid and discuss important things (blessed pack aside.) But as a way to have official material discussing the non-homid breeds without someone bringing up Ways of the Wolf, it failed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T04:13:19-08:00","id":1427553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427528#post1427528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ret-con of Avatar storm and the Malady is also an added content.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you elaborate further on this topics, please.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427533#post1427533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... let's just assume they were infected by Wyrm or mind-wiped by Nephandi...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah,... A Wizard did it!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T05:20:48-08:00","id":1427567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427553#post1427553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you elaborate further on this topics, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a sidebar somewhere like &quot;Future Fates: the Umbra&quot;, pg. 37.<br /> <br /> Avatar Storm &quot;now&quot; affects Garou, causing a lethal damage per cross (aggravated with fail or botch) and the Gauntlet increases by 1.<br /> <br /> Malady is the spiritual side of global warming. Gaia goes into slumber, and the Gauntlet thickens more. +3 (additional to the Awatar Storm stuff) to the Gauntlet. You can't cross if it goes above 9.<br /> <br /> You can do a 5 minute &quot;meditation&quot; to decrease the Gauntled by 1.<br /> <br /> This means you almost can't step sideway.<br /> <br /> WW 5e. refers to the Malady, so I think this addon was intentional to guide towards the waited/feared new edition.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T06:08:24-08:00","id":1427577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427567#post1427567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WW 5e. refers to the Malady, so I think this addon was intentional to guide towards the waited/feared new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there already parts of WW5 available?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T06:26:05-08:00","id":1427582,"title":"","content":"From the WW5e prewiew page:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:brandon-grot-w01-light\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The <b>Malady </b>is rampant, and Rage, as with most weapons, can cut both ways. It is a dark time for the dying Garou, while the primordial forces of the <b>Weaver and the Wyrm continue to grow</b>, and the essence of the <b>Wyld fades</b> with every passing year.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The <b>Malady </b>brings with it growing internal <b>resistance</b>, the <b>Gauntlet </b>begins to <b>harden</b>, and the past itself ripples back in echoes to haunt the Garou of tonight.&quot;</span></span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T13:32:21-08:00","id":1427628,"title":"","content":"Though W5 is now under an entirely new development team....so possibly that garbage might be gone....though it feels really weird to be relying on Parawolf to NOT insert nonsense and edgy garbage into a product. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T13:35:05-08:00","id":1427629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427628#post1427628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though W5 is now under an entirely new development team....so possibly that garbage might be gone....though it feels really weird to be relying on Parawolf to NOT insert nonsense and edgy garbage into a product. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well we all saw how that worked out with V5.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T14:34:41-08:00","id":1427635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427567#post1427567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a sidebar somewhere like &quot;Future Fates: the Umbra&quot;, pg. 37.<br /> <br /> Avatar Storm &quot;now&quot; affects Garou, causing a lethal damage per cross (aggravated with fail or botch) and the Gauntlet increases by 1.<br /> <br /> Malady is the spiritual side of global warming. Gaia goes into slumber, and the Gauntlet thickens more. +3 (additional to the Awatar Storm stuff) to the Gauntlet. You can't cross if it goes above 9.<br /> <br /> You can do a 5 minute &quot;meditation&quot; to decrease the Gauntled by 1.<br /> <br /> This means you almost can't step sideway.<br /> <br /> WW 5e. refers to the Malady, so I think this addon was intentional to guide towards the waited/feared new edition.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All of this just sounds, really, really, horrible. The Umbra was literally the best part of Werewolf and for me personally; all of oWoD. I felt the Avatar Storm from Mage really was stupid.. and to see aspects of this philosophy in Werewolf officially/RAW really bums me out. Why do they think this is a good idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T14:53:32-08:00","id":1427639,"title":"","content":"nWW and now Paradox seemed to have learned all of the wrong lessons from the CofD in their attempts to update the WoD. I can unpack this more, but not enough time right now. But this extends all over the place from changes to mechanics and lore, to overvaluing the opinions of specific sub-communities within the general *oD fandom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T17:10:18-08:00","id":1427650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427546#post1427546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lore content of the game is generally not something I need for my games. However the book does have a lot of decent mechanical stuff: rules for what it takes to do body modification on a Garou, the custom pack tactics, the new rites and Gifts. The new Metis deformities are... hit or miss thematically, but the mechanics tend to be fine. The section on coming up with new rites and modifying existing ones is fairy sparse on the mechanical side of things (though I can't really blame them, as the official Rites are a mechanical nightmare of inconsistency) but it's still a solid part of the book.<br /> <br /> So it gets a solid, &quot;mechanics from CW20 assume yes, lore from CW20 assume no,&quot; for my games.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's unfortunate that when faced with a book that someone deliberately made transphobic, the response is &quot;use these parts but ignore those parts&quot; and not &quot;it's better to skip this book.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427639#post1427639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">nWW and now Paradox seemed to have learned all of the wrong lessons from the CofD in their attempts to update the WoD. I can unpack this more, but not enough time right now. But this extends all over the place from changes to mechanics and lore, to overvaluing the opinions of specific sub-communities within the general *oD fandom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which specific subcommunities?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T19:11:17-08:00","id":1427663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427650#post1427650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's unfortunate that when faced with a book that someone deliberately made transphobic, the response is &quot;use these parts but ignore those parts&quot; and not &quot;it's better to skip this book.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I bought the book before I was aware of the problems. I can't deny Paradox money to protest their actions. Since it's too late for me to spend my RPG budget on a book without such problems, I'm not harming people by making it clear that the book is highly problematic, but there's bits that can be excised successfully for use in games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which specific subcommunities? </div> </div> </div>Specific large WoD LARP organizations. I'm not sure it's helpful to get into specifics beyond that. The leaders of one were very influential on the start of the nWoD on what sort of changes fans would stay on board for: resulting in the fairly bland VtR 1e and WtF 1e corebooks, and the CofD not really becoming it's own thing until later releases. The BNS MET groups are likewise getting a lot more of Paradox's ear (Jason Carl being hired by them doesn't help) as speaking for far more of the fandom than they have a right to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T03:03:23-08:00","id":1427687,"title":"","content":"I share Heavy Arms' concerns. A lot of the changes I saw in BNS's WtA seem to cater to the needs of LARP games, especially satisfying the need of players to get special snowflakes by creating rule that specifically incorporate the ability to create fera into the game and make them more compatible with the garou. In my opinion the game should have been &quot;BNS's Were-whatever: Age of Apocalypse&quot; rather than WtA. Any I really hope WW5e doesn't become that ... unrecognisable.<br /> <br /> As for the Avatar Storm and Malady. W20 already put hard constrains on stepping sideways. The need for a mirror returned and portable mirrors are at +1 difficulty. So, mighty get of fenris will kick open the gas station restroom door to use the mirror there instead of carrying a make-up mirror in their man-purse.<br /> I would have ignored Avatar Storm and Malady, well, that certain areas have higher Gauntlet ratings when weaver-like is known, that now there are areas devastated by global warming, which suffer also Gauntlet increases is okay, if it doesn't have any stupid amount of focus in the game.<br /> Also, I found that steppung Sideways should have reworked anyways. Difficulties should be limited to a smaller range, like 5 to 8. Also, it should take relatively long but not with a spread between 1 round to 10 minutes. Although, I go with WoD:Combat, that after 3 rounds the garou are &quot;in transit&quot; and have successfully disappeared where they were, but not yet appeared where they want to go.<br /> Returning to the need of mirrors, in my opinion, was a mistake. It should be allowed to initiate stepping sideways with meditation alone.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Is there open development somewhere?<br /> I didn't find any meaningful information on the hunters entertainment website.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T03:47:55-08:00","id":1427691,"title":"","content":"I've always house-ruled and done it where you can side-step anywhere as long as you have some Gnosis in your system. All that would really stop you is the local Gauntlet level if its really high and if you keep getting failed rolls for it. The fact is that the Garou in many situations NEED to get into the Umbra fast and its silly that you need meditation or a long wait time to warp into it.<br /> <br /> That Bane that had just materialized and killed a bunch of hikers, then went back into the Umbra? Oh, we need to tail it fast? Oh right... we need mirrors and/or we need to wait awhile.. by the time they get into the Umbra, that Bane is already long gone. So in short, the entire namesake of <b><i>Side</i></b>-STEP should relatively be a fast on the fly movement. Constricting or making it tedious doesn't make sense since the Umbra is so integral for this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T03:54:39-08:00","id":1427692,"title":"","content":"The Malady truly sounds like whoever wrote it never used Umbra much in their games and so did not see the point of having easy access to it. That and the BNS destruction of MOST Caerns and making Caerns harder to make. If that is your thing, cool. But to me, a huge part of WtA is spirituality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T04:52:23-08:00","id":1427696,"title":"","content":"I think that the need to enter the penumbra fast is kind of academic. If you don't allow spirits to materialise and de-materialise as they please, then your scenario is mood, but if the access was in a timeframe of minutes rather than seconds, it wouldn't hinder the garou as much, but still prohibit the penumbra as means of bypassing material obstacles like vault doors, machine gun nests and such...<br /> The decision to move through the Gauntlet would have more meaning strategically.<br /> <br /> What I gathered from BNS's WtA was that pretty much everyone could get a Caern Shard and try to use it to plant a new caern by tending to it. In theory much easier than a Caern Building Rite with all the supernaturals in the area becoming aware of it to some degree. But, it also shifted, or is intended to shift, the focus from a sept as base of operations to a pack who have their 'hood to protect. Much like WtF.<br /> I was never a fan of revised Editions globalisation of the garou nation focus, but always favoured the 2nd edtion focus on regional septs as the foundation of a chronicle and garou society as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T10:46:47-08:00","id":1427727,"title":"","content":"I've found BNS at least intresting. Even tried to ST in it, as it moved the timeline forward in an acceptable way.<br /> <br /> I don't like the thickening Gauntlet, but at least the Banes are not much a problem. They can't just materialize in the closet..., except in caerns.<br /> <br /> I've bought the Chainging Ways, but I was very unsatisfied with the product. By the way I agree with HeavyArms. System ok, fluff... not. But at least I've bought a product from my favourite game line, which may help it live longer.<br /> Still it may lead to utter disaster (like V5, and not because of the controversy).<br /> <br /> About playing Fera. I'm a fan of Kitsune. I'm currently playing one tabletop. If the ST and the players can handle the Fera well, it can go into an intresting story. Of course if anybody plays anything, but Garou, it's an other thing.<br /> <br /> I *think* the BNS handles the think in an acceptable level. You can be Fera, and partialy you can be accepted, but the Sanctum of Gaia will make you a subordinate or kick your buttocks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T13:05:06-08:00","id":1427742,"title":"","content":"I like playing Fera too, in tabletop, and if the troupe is okay with that, it's perfectly good and fun. But a group of Fera, especially a mixed-fera group like the Ahadi or Hengeyokai plays very differently than a pack of garou. If I want to play WtA that isn't what I expect. If I play in a larger LARP, that's also what I would expect from all the players. In White Wolf's MET Fera were the exception in BNS it is a core rules option where a merit allows to be a fera character - this leads to players feeling that they have a right to those characters and makes STs the bad guys (or fellow players) if they opt for a classical garou centered game.<br /> <br /> Playing Fera like playing Kinfolk is a variant of the game, much like playing Anarchs, Sabbat or Assamites is a variation in VtM, or playing Technocracy would be a variation of MtA. They are perfectly good games if all players are on board with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T13:23:03-08:00","id":1427745,"title":"","content":"The BNS MET books were created during the 20th design era with the same concept of being big omnibus editions that include as much of the playable material as possible (and most of the Fera were KS based stretch goals at that).<br /> <br /> The &quot;use Merits to play rare character types&quot; thing is something that's already part of the rules of many of the big LARP organizations (going back to one of my previous points) use to coordinate play across multiple local games. The bigger WtA LARP groups also tend to down play the Umbra a lot because it's exceedingly impractical for LARP play past a certain group size.<br /> <br /> And there's also, again, the wrong lessons from Forsaken here. Forsaken makes it fairly difficult to get into the Shadow outside of a Locus. But this is to serve Forsaken's specific and different themes. Loci are far more common than Caerns, but far less powerful, making them more appropriate as pack-controlled phenomenon; and grounds for pack-based territorial disputes. The Shadow is also not friendly territory to the Forsaken, even before you get to corrupted parts. Going into the Shadow is something you do frequently, but its a Big Deal, not done lightly.<br /> <br /> Making WtA operate more like WtF in regards to access to the Umbra doesn't mesh with the idea that the Garou have a significantly better relationship with their spiritual world by default.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T17:35:08-08:00","id":1427780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427745#post1427745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And there's also, again, the wrong lessons from Forsaken here. Forsaken makes it fairly difficult to get into the Shadow outside of a Locus. But this is to serve Forsaken's specific and different themes. Loci are far more common than Caerns, but far less powerful, making them more appropriate as pack-controlled phenomenon; and grounds for pack-based territorial disputes. The Shadow is also not friendly territory to the Forsaken, even before you get to corrupted parts. Going into the Shadow is something you do frequently, but its a Big Deal, not done lightly.<br /> <br /> Making WtA operate more like WtF in regards to access to the Umbra doesn't mesh with the idea that the Garou have a significantly better relationship with their spiritual world by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention, if Caerns go, there goes most of garou society. Yes, you CAN have septs without a Caern, but certain rites -need- Caerns to work. Metis are still a thing as are lupus, so suddenly you have lil' Veil Breach and Scooby Doo there without the protection of the Veil.<br /> <br /> Nevermind all the other things such as easy access to ritualists, common gathering spot,etc. And the whole theme of epic horror fantasy that WtA has.<br /> <br /> Also, the Uratha are not on a time limit. They might be hated by the hisil and the pure, but they don't have a ticking clock over them where every failure is costly to the ENTIRE world. Hence why Caerns and the umbra suffering IS basically game over for the garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T21:52:04-08:00","id":1427807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;use Merits to play rare character types&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. So was this logic and idea incorporated with how the &quot;Hecata&quot; were handled in regards to how they're a &quot;Sect&quot;, but really a Clan; but if you want to play as the pre-V5 bloodlines (Nagaraja, Samedi, Harbinger, etc.), its relegated to a merit? That explains a lot then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T23:45:10-08:00","id":1427817,"title":"","content":"I can't speak directly to that decision, but it's very in-keeping with how the larger LARP organizations tended to handle a lot of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T23:50:03-08:00","id":1427818,"title":"","content":"Well, with caern gone, the sept's gathering places and the caern infrastructure (assembly area, shrines, housing area, etc.) will still be there, just lacking the caern heart and the supernatural aspect of the place. Also reducing the need for packs to protect the place is reduced and the renown gain from being warder or guardian would be lowered, because their jobs become less essential. But there would still be places to live for lupus and metis born garou...<br /> <br /> Still, I don't like the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T00:07:51-08:00","id":1427820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427818#post1427818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, with caern gone, the sept's gathering places and the caern infrastructure (assembly area, shrines, housing area, etc.) will still be there, just lacking the caern heart and the supernatural aspect of the place. Also reducing the need for packs to protect the place is reduced and the renown gain from being warder or guardian would be lowered, because their jobs become less essential. But there would still be places to live for lupus and metis born garou...<br /> <br /> Still, I don't like the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only those places wouldn't have the spiritual 'human don't come here' that Caerns have. Without a Caern and thus without such a close tie to the spirits, a human could EASILY waltz into Caern lands. Delirium is a thing, sure, but only so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T00:19:32-08:00","id":1427822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427820#post1427820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only those places wouldn't have the spiritual 'human don't come here' that Caerns have. Without a Caern and thus without such a close tie to the spirits, a human could EASILY waltz into Caern lands. Delirium is a thing, sure, but only so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do Caerns have innate &quot;Humans don't come here&quot; qualities? Is there a page reference to that?<br /> I mean, I gather that each full moon, for possibly centuries, the Revel will lead a hoard of marauding garou through the adjacent woods, in Crinos, wrecking havoc of sorts, and that humans won't go there. But this, I gather, is due to the Rage spend there and in general the Rage concentration around garou caerns, but not the caern itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T01:33:12-08:00","id":1427829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427822#post1427822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Caerns have innate &quot;Humans don't come here&quot; qualities? Is there a page reference to that?<br /> I mean, I gather that each full moon, for possibly centuries, the Revel will lead a hoard of marauding garou through the adjacent woods, in Crinos, wrecking havoc of sorts, and that humans won't go there. But this, I gather, is due to the Rage spend there and in general the Rage concentration around garou caerns, but not the caern itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are rites upon rites hiding a Caern's presence. Bone Gnawers have two rites dedicated to ensuring Caern safety (Signpost and No Trespassing), and I'm pretty sure other tribes have such methods as well.<br /> <br /> Then there are spirit guardians on the umbral side, physical guardians using their spiritual allies,etc. Rite of Enchanted Forest too can be used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T02:58:17-08:00","id":1427832,"title":"","content":"In BNS the Caerns do not totaly vanish.<br /> Yeh, main, old caerns remain only in handful, but there are shard-caerns.<br /> <br /> About having one Shard Caern (SC): It's unknown how many shards the main caerns grow. I'd rule, not more than Level.<br /> Shards can be stolen, and there are now two fighting fragments of the Garou Nations.<br /> In my headcannon, the protection of Shards should be a hight priority.<br /> <br /> Norturing them, another. I see lot'sa possibilities in this part of BNS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T03:26:35-08:00","id":1427834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427829#post1427829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are rites upon rites hiding a Caern's presence. Bone Gnawers have two rites dedicated to ensuring Caern safety (Signpost and No Trespassing), and I'm pretty sure other tribes have such methods as well.<br /> <br /> Then there are spirit guardians on the umbral side, physical guardians using their spiritual allies,etc. Rite of Enchanted Forest too can be used.</div> </div> </div> </div>One could assume so, but in the rules (pre-W20) there is only<ul><li><i>Warding the Lingering Human - </i>Which protects from Wraith</li> <li><i>Rite of the Shrouded Glen</i> - which protects from divination, umbral travel, and the Rite of Luna's Spear.</li> </ul><br /> that are explicitly Caern Rites.<br /> <i>Signpost</i> is a mystical Rite, but you are right, it has special rules when enacted for a caern. So, sure, this one is a proper defensive tool. <i>No Tresspassing</i> essentially does the same for rural Bone Gnawer caerns. Bur are there really variant for other tribes?<br /> I haven't read any indication, although it would makes some sense...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T03:47:03-08:00","id":1427836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427832#post1427832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In BNS the Caerns do not totaly vanish.<br /> Yeh, main, old caerns remain only in handful, but there are shard-caerns.<br /> <br /> About having one Shard Caern (SC): It's unknown how many shards the main caerns grow. I'd rule, not more than Level.<br /> Shards can be stolen, and there are now two fighting fragments of the Garou Nations.<br /> In my headcannon, the protection of Shards should be a hight priority.<br /> <br /> Norturing them, another. I see lot'sa possibilities in this part of BNS.</div> </div> </div> </div>So they added yet another McGuffin to a game that already has a plethora of them? Wait....so Caerns are succulent plants now? Why do I need a part of a Wisdom Caern from the US dedicated to White Buffalo Woman in order to create a Rage Caern dedicated to Taipan? Why would I not rather find a naturally occurring djang site, aspect it over time to reflect the correct spiritual synchronicity, form alliances and intense political sessions spent suppressing opposition and preventing interference from third parties and then perform the arduous and taxing rite to try and awaken the Caern. Why am I reliant on a 'magic rock'? Did I accidentally wander in from Forsaken? Nope...yet another 'solution' desperately looking for a non-existent problem from BNS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T04:12:43-08:00","id":1427837,"title":"","content":"Yes, I feel a lot of changes in W20 and BNS's WtA try to fix something, that I feed wasn't broken (in revised).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T04:39:12-08:00","id":1427838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427836#post1427836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So they added yet another McGuffin to a game that already has a plethora of them? Wait....so Caerns are succulent plants now? Why do I need a part of a Wisdom Caern from the US dedicated to White Buffalo Woman in order to create a Rage Caern dedicated to Taipan? Why would I not rather find a naturally occurring djang site, aspect it over time to reflect the correct spiritual synchronicity, form alliances and intense political sessions spent suppressing opposition and preventing interference from third parties and then perform the arduous and taxing rite to try and awaken the Caern. Why am I reliant on a 'magic rock'? Did I accidentally wander in from Forsaken? Nope...yet another 'solution' desperately looking for a non-existent problem from BNS.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree with you. This can be / was / will be (who knows?) a good scenario also.<br /> <br /> For me both solutions are acceptable. We don't know, what versions, timeline, backgorund will be accepted. System is also foggy. We shall see.<br /> <br /> All I know that there are matching info in BNS &amp; what I've found on Hunter's page, so I'm a little bit suspicious.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I did in tabletop:<br /> Started a story based on BNS, will use the Shattered Dreams and leed my players into an official timeline at the end. Until than they will'll play Slider on drugs in Time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T08:38:49-08:00","id":1427862,"title":"","content":"The LARP and Tabletop aspect of the game should have separate universes and mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T08:47:50-08:00","id":1427865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427862#post1427862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The LARP and Tabletop aspect of the game should have separate universes and mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, mechanics yes, meta no. If table top games become to big you can transition to larps and vice versa if the larp shrinks to a small group. Met made conversion rules back in the day for a reason. <br /> <br /> Also who wants to learn two different metas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T08:56:10-08:00","id":1427867,"title":"","content":"I also wouldn't think of two universes. Well, each chronicle or alliance of chronicles is it's own universe.<br /> But, we play WtA LARP to play WtA and not another game. We wouldn't want to have any Setting different from revised, anyway.<br /> <br /> However, there are certainly different requirements to the game system, and also fluff to some degree. A lot of things that are handwaved in tabletop or simply resolved by a roll, need to be acted in LARP, and therefore descriptions of a lot of things need to be fleshed out by players considerably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T08:58:52-08:00","id":1427868,"title":"","content":"Alright whole different meta is too much, but mechanics have to be different. LARP and Tabletop have very different playstyles. LARP is more physical and more larger in imagination, while Tabletop is more about sitting down and everything is miniaturized. That's why the Umbra is downplayed or disregarded in LARP, while the Umbra is able to be done more better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T14:47:28-08:00","id":1427910,"title":"","content":"I think LARP and Tabletop should be seperate if the LARP IC meta changes in order to make things easier for LARP STs and organisers OOC which is what BNS did. Its why they now have a simple Camarilla/Sabbat type division among the Tribes, little to no Umbral Access, Bites turning Kinfolk into Garou, removal of all barriers to Tribal membership because it makes the paperwork and recruitment easier for those running and playing and has nothing to do with the integrity of the In Universe meta-physics and setting.<br /> <br /> Because at the moment LARP is driving everything about WoD Tabletop design despite being a much smaller player base. And in case it needs to be said, I'm not shitting on LARP, I've done it in the past and it was fun though more than a little pretentious. I doubt I could do it these days, it was hard enough suspending belief that a bunch of badly dressed out of shape teens and twenties were immortal creatures of the night. Seeing a bunch of 40 and 50 year olds doing it will just be sad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T15:22:36-08:00","id":1427913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bites turning Kinfolk into Garou</div> </div> </div> </div>WHAT......LMAO","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T16:34:45-08:00","id":1427920,"title":"","content":"While a lot of people don't like the addition of the Bitten... I think it was better handled that you might expect.<br /> <br /> It's actually the first successful attempt to make the &quot;Meits shock troops&quot; concept make sense, as the Bitten (while mechanically the Breed of their birth) are sterile, but can actually be produced in numbers. Though those numbers require giving up a lot of kinfolk that don't survive it.<br /> <br /> Introducing bite-based werewolves to WtA is something that most people aren't going to get past, but it's actually horrific (in a good way for a horror setting) addition in its implications. The BSDs can have their kinfolk have a bunch of kids while young, and then bite them to turn some of them into shock troops and toss the corpses of the rest. This actually puts the Gaians in a position where their morals and their goals are hard to line up. The BSDs can flood the field with new bodies without resorting to Metis (the Bite takes 28 days to set in, so hey can even pick which Auspices they want more of). If the Garou don't start using their kinfolk even worse than they did before, they're going to get swamped. If they do, they're probably going to doom themselves in the long term.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to argue about whether it is a good or bad thing to put into WtA this far into the game's existence, but the concept itself is actually pretty solid.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T17:38:10-08:00","id":1427925,"title":"","content":"I see your point, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>.<br /> The ability becomes even more frightening, when the BSD snatch (probably not yet 'Kenning') young kinfolk of other tribes and turn them into Bitten. I didn't realise they were sterile before. For me it always seemed like forcing the &quot;being bitten&quot; werewolf mythology into WtA and kind of copying the Birthing Plague in the process.<br /> The moral dilemma that comes with this eluded me, probably because I missed the sterile information and what the consequences of this are.<br /> <br /> But, even more as W20's &quot;you can't determine the difference between kinfolk and pre-change garou&quot; this totally changes the kinfolk/gaou relationship. From discussions I had with BNS authors at the Grand Masquerade in NOLA (or was it Berlin), was that they thought that the treatment of kinfolk, especially women kinfolk, by the garou gave WtA a bad reputation. So, this changes might also factor into this need to make anything accessible to everyone, kind of.<br /> <br /> However, there is a reality that people aren't equal, and that categorizing, and by extension thinking of archetypes and prejudices, help us to make sense of the world. While it makes sense to challenge one's own believes and prejudices regularly, it doesn't make sense to force the disruptions of such archetypes as tribes present into the game. For, the tribes should provide character creation and gameplay advice by providing archetypes - if they didn't they were pointless. Therefore the removal of restrictions regarding the entry into tribes is counter productive.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T17:50:01-08:00","id":1427926,"title":"","content":"The concept is horrible and hilarious. By the time a first wave is dispatched and the BSD retreat to lick their wounds, all the Gaian Garou will do is hunt down and just plain kill the BSD kinfolk in the area to stop such a tactic from being done again. It's also a waste of time because you'd presumably still not have many who actually succeed in transforming with the &quot;Bitten&quot; effect, while only a milquetoast number batch still standing. It's literally the same as if having a regular Metis, but with the worst aspect of literally killing your own supply of Kinfolk that can birth conducive Garou.<br /> <br /> Also quantity doesn't matter when these Kinfolk-turned-Garou would be so inexperienced in combat and transforming it would be a breeze dispatching them once the alarm around a local Garou society is alerted and all the Packs form up into one force. Shocktroops aren't about listless mass numbers, but about quality, experience, and deadliness. BSD use their Metis as such because from birth they are very experienced in Crinos naturally and can be trained in fighting forms in it across their development. It also isn't a net loss for the BSD to use Metis as Shocktroops because their sterile, while a loss from a Kinfolk-turned-Garou is an extreme loss; more so than losing a regular natural Garou, for the sheer fact how much Kinfolk are important to continuing Garou population.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 12-09-2020, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T18:01:03-08:00","id":1427927,"title":"","content":"If Garou could just find BSD Kinfolk by opening the phonebook, you were right. But BSD tend to be rapists, and have been so for centuries. So, pretty much every human who's parents, grandparents or great-grandparents suffered from sexualised violence that turned into a pregnancy could be BDS kinfolk. And with adoption, the stigma of talking about it and several other factors, they are pretty much unfindable. I mean, the BSD have a certain subculture, but it's not necessarily as obvious as that of garou tribe kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't know what the odds of survival for the Bitten are. Do you? Please, elaborate.<br /> <br /> Turning a kinfolk into an garou in 28 days and then spend a year or two in training still beats a metis brith by two to three years. Also, the metis is, depending on source material used, more likely to kill the mother during child birth, so it doesn't male sense for BSD females to carry a metis, but one would have to limit this to the rape of captured female garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T18:01:43-08:00","id":1427928,"title":"","content":"Yeah, its garbage. Its basically just some Sabbat LARP ST going &quot; What if we had Werewolf shovelheads!! lol!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T18:13:17-08:00","id":1427929,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that the Bitten are physically and spiritually sterile: they can't perform the Bite any more than can have kids (after the Bite).<br /> <br /> Though it works on more than Kinfolk, it also works on pre-Change Garou and something BNS calls the Unborn (Garou that never change for whatever reason)... adding more questionable issues. What if you accidentally sterilize a late change Garou? The BSDs might not care, but the Gaian Garou certainly would.<br /> <br /> The odds of survival (for potential Bitten) is left vague in the book because it's supposed to be a very recent phenomenon, and most Bitten were Kinfolk that survived BSD attacks, with the second wave of them being BSD purposefully made ones after they figured it out (the Garou Nation tried to hide it at first but realized it wouldn't last, so there hasn't been any major wave of Gaian Bitten purposefully made... yet). It's implied that ~10% survived the original wave of them, but after people realized what was going on, if you have good enough Theurges around you can get the survival rate to ~50%, but some of them are going to snap from the experience and get stuck in a permanent Frenzy (something again, the BSDs are perfectly happy to consider a success that the Gaians aren't).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T18:18:56-08:00","id":1427930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Turning a kinfolk into an garou in 28 days and then spend a year or two in training still beats a metis brith by two to three years.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really depends on the first wave. Once the Garou in the region know the BSD are doing a Bitten tactic, almost all of the Septs in a state or more will prowl the area and just clean house. And again, Metis BSD are better Shocktroops still because they would be trained from birth more extensively. Two to three years of training once an amassed numbers of ranked Andren to Elder begin going on a warpath isn't enough for BSD-Bitten, they still would be relatively inexperienced. It also isn't worth it to cut into Kinfolk numbers.<br /> <br /> Also Kinfolk are general. There isn't really any specific &quot;tribe&quot; of Kinfolk technically. A Kinfolk born from rape by a BSD and forgotten about later down the line is just a regular Kinfolk forgotten about. If the Garou kill the main Kinfolk in the BSD's general holdings/territory, it may take years to gather a whole new network of them. The Bitten tactic just isn't worth it and in general clashes with WTA's themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 12-09-2020, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T18:36:33-08:00","id":1427933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427920#post1427920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Introducing bite-based werewolves to WtA is something that most people aren't going to get past...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. While one could just rest on that being the Ratkin's bag, W:tA was also pointedly free of a lot of common werewolf tropes used in pop culture, the bite causing the development of lycanthropy being among them. The closest that one got was the Curse of the Wolf punishment rite from Werewolf: the Dark Ages, and that didn't turn the hapless human target into an actual werewolf, unless one starts and ends their definition of werewolf as &quot;enter Crinos during full moon, kill everyone and everything around&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T01:55:02-08:00","id":1427948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427930#post1427930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Kinfolk are general. There isn't really any specific &quot;tribe&quot; of Kinfolk technically. A Kinfolk born from rape by a BSD and forgotten about later down the line is just a regular Kinfolk forgotten about. If the Garou kill the main Kinfolk in the BSD's general holdings/territory, it may take years to gather a whole new network of them. The Bitten tactic just isn't worth it and in general clashes with WTA's themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Silver Fang Kinfolk needs a point of Pure Breed according to &quot;Unsung Heroes&quot;.<br /> <br /> But, you are right, mechanically or supernaturally there might not be any tribe related characteristic in a kinfok, besides a 5XP discount on Gift purchases for Gifts that are considered in-house for the tribe. But, tribes incorporate kinfolk and kinfolk associates themselves with tribes. If one Monday morning the a pack of BSD goes to rent a large truck and then goes on snatching each garou kinfolk ages fifteen to thirty they know of, hide them in a place warded from divination (so Questing Stone and Sense of Prey won't lead the garou there) they can turn, torture and brainwash a lot of new recruits. Those stuck in permanent frenzy, they just need to keep locked up and throw a t-bone steak into their cages very now and then. The rest can be corrupted by other means. Even without Gifts these guys get the significant Crinos form bonuses to and the Garou probably will try to find ways to safe then, employing non-lethal force. In any case, they are an adequate distraction, so the BSD can sneak up behind the garou...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T03:35:51-08:00","id":1427952,"title":"","content":"One point, you missed about the bitten: don't work for BSDs.<br /> <br /> For me, this was first confusing, but could adopt to be a brick for good adventures. All in all, it turned to be a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T04:30:06-08:00","id":1427956,"title":"","content":"The Bite works for BSDs on Kinfolk, it doesn't work for them on Unborn (which is actually in their favor if you think about it, because it means they can't screw up and accidentally use the Bite on a late change/stalled Garou like the Gaians can, though there's still a good chance the Unborn dies).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T07:48:52-08:00","id":1427974,"title":"","content":"Why does it work differently for BSD than for other garou?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T13:55:46-08:00","id":1428025,"title":"","content":"I don't like the Bitten as a concept in the setting.<br /> <br /> I understand why they did it - the idea of a werewolf biting someone to cause them to turn into a werewolf is now a part of popular culture as a result of many movies (though this was never part of actual folklore). So there are people who think this is something that needs to be included in the setting.<br /> <br /> However, I incorporated that in my game by simply having it be a way for Garou to help &quot;force&quot; the First Change upon a pre-change &quot;cub&quot;, especially those Garou who are &quot;lost&quot; and were raised in an unknowing family. It's along the lines that the Garou know this person should change, but hasn't yet. And this is something that sometimes works to prompt the change in cases where that Garou is somehow suppressing the wolf. Besides biting, I included many other things that may &quot;force&quot; the First Change which correspond to many other ways in folklore and pop culture that describe how one &quot;becomes&quot; a werewolf.<br /> <br /> So I don't see the need for the Bitten. I think it undermines and contradicts too much established lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-10T14:22:41-08:00","id":1428027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1427974#post1427974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does it work differently for BSD than for other garou?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is explicitly left to be a mystery.<br /> <br /> The book states that the common thought is that the Bite is connected to Gaia in someway. Kinfolk, even BSDs one, still have a spiritual connection to Gaia that the BSDs don't after dancing the Spiral and dedicating themselves purely to the Wyrm, while the Unborn (a new phenomenon as well) might be stalled Garou because their spiritual connection to Gaia is blocked in someway. So Unborn's lack of connection to Gaia + BSD = no Bitten produced (though the Bite can still occur), while Kinfolk still having some spiritual spark of Gaia in them + BSD = potential Bitten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T10:51:27-08:00","id":1428369,"title":"","content":"UGH the more I read about BNS, the more clear it is that it's not WtA anymore.<br /> If people want to play a WtF Larp, then just write a WtF Larp and call it WtF! Then the WtF fans would know where to find it. If they seriously want to merge the two settings into a jumbled incoherent mess with no clear themes, they should at least call it by a new name, not pretend it's Apocalypse. When Monte Cook made a new version of the WoD, he didn't claim it was cWoD or CofD because it wasn't.<br /> <br /> If a local ST offered to run a Werewolf: the Apocalypse LARP, and then used this instead, it would be a bait-and-switch and I'd be quite upset at being duped.<br /> <br /> And removing the Umbra from W5 is the worst, most BS idea possible. I think they're doing this so they can make a video game more easily, set 90% on Earth and/or with nothing beyond the Penumbra or Periphery. Any video game is pretty much guaranteed to be more popular than the tabletop so they have no reason to care about the tabletop quality or audience. They could alienate literally every tabletop player on Earth and still be reasonably assured they'll make a bigger profit on video games than the real WW ever did in the 90s.<br /> <br /> I certainly will switch solely to Storyteller's Vault products.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 12-14-2020, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-14T11:19:08-08:00","id":1428375,"title":"","content":"I would think, Penumbra would be enough for a Computergame, but I would be hard to have the penumbra feeling conveyed satisfactorily. There have been plenty of parallel world puzzles in adventure games (Legend of Zelda comes to mind right away) and the umbra should be more than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T13:03:44-08:00","id":1428503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1428369#post1428369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If people want to play a WtF Larp, then just write a WtF Larp and call it WtF!</div> </div> </div> </div>The BNS version of WtA is nothing to do with WtF. It\u2019s not a WtF larp. It may have increasingly distant resemblance to ttrpg WtA but that\u2019s still its setting.<br /> <br /> The decision makers at White Wolf (before it dissolved back into Paradox) wanted ttrpg WtA to be more like larp WtA, which was the origin of several of the changes imposed onto the rpg books. I have no idea how the new in-house W5 will bring together the diverging lore and assumptions between the two, if at all, but it won\u2019t be WtF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T13:34:29-08:00","id":1428504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1428503#post1428503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The BNS version of WtA is nothing to do with WtF. It\u2019s not a WtF larp. It may have increasingly distant resemblance to ttrpg WtA but that\u2019s still its setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It derived from tabletop WtA but it is arguably not the same Setting any more. It isn't WtF either, but is seems to try to incorporate some elements of WtF.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't call it WtF LARP, either. I'd call it &quot;Age of Apocalypse&quot; LARP.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T14:22:03-08:00","id":1428511,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what elements it's actually incorporating from WtF. The whole Shard Caern thing, bringing the Avatar Storm to WtA, and the Bitten might have a few superficial similarities to aspects of Forsaken, but nothing as direct as V5 using Touchstones.<br /> <br /> Of course, I'm pretty sure the House of Mouse would sue if you actually tried to call something the Age of Apocalypse LARP (since that was the title of a Marvel based comic event a while ago).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T15:46:47-08:00","id":1428516,"title":"","content":"&quot;Age of Apocalypse&quot; was 1995 and I can't see if the name was trademarked. In any case &quot;Werewolf: Age of Apocalypse&quot; might be sufficiently removed from &quot;X-Men: Age of Apocalypse&quot;. That is despite the fact Marvel also has a comic title called &quot;Werewolf&quot;. A LARP game might also be sufficiently removed from a comic book story line to not pose a problem. But I'm no trademark lawyer.<br /> <br /> <br /> In any case, I find that the Setting is too far removed from WtA's revised that it should still be allowed to be called that. And I hope WW5e isn't the that way....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-15T16:25:38-08:00","id":1428521,"title":"","content":"It was mostly a jab at how litigious Disney is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-18T11:21:42-08:00","id":1432618,"title":"","content":"Werewolf: the Apocalypse with no Umbra and no caerns is fundamentally not the same game. It doesn't even resemble being the same gameline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-19T13:56:28-08:00","id":1432715,"title":"","content":"So after seeing this thread a little while back I started reading changing ways (thinking &quot;how bad can it be?)<br /> <br /> -While the trans stuff leaves much to be desired, is it really that bad? Reading this thread, it sounds like the book's full of hate. I've only read this little bit, and it seems like someone who didn't want to talk about trans people was made to talk about trans people and they got weird with the -Garou don't like it because it's unnatural / But also if you just ask a spirit you can change and it's dead easy- <br /> Look, it's definitely not good, and If I channel the ghost of a Conservative I'm also left unsatisfied, I get that it's an issue people are very sensitive about; but it's not a huge glaring section of hate like suggested here. Skimming through the book, there seems to be a lot of reaching out to the LGB community (The 'Social butterfly' gift seems pretty hamfisted) and it doesn't land well, but honestly from reading some of the comments I expected it to be a <i>lot </i>worse. <br /> <br /> <br /> Secondly, was this 'malady and betrayal' part of some plotline I haven't read? The book acts like it's a thing I should've heard of. I've read a lot of werewolf and I don't know it. (which could be my fault but I don't read books of metaplot or city books or anything like that)<br /> <br /> <br /> -Where's this 'bitten thing you're all talking about? Where is that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-19T14:20:08-08:00","id":1432718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1432715#post1432715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Where's this 'bitten thing you're all talking about? Where is that?</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't in &quot;Changing Ways&quot; (which is form OPP's W20 line and a book for tabletop WtA) but it is from &quot;Mind's Eye Theatre: Werewolf the Apocalpyse&quot; by &quot;By Night Studios&quot; (BNS), and it is a &quot;Live Action Role Playing&quot; (LARP) rules book.<br /> <br /> W20 was created after CCP closed the White Wolf offices in Atlanta and OPP was created. OPP was (and still is) licensing what then was called &quot;classic World of Darkness&quot; (cWoD). But OPP only had/has licenses for tabletop RPG and, if I'm not mistaken, occasionally merchandise (on a case to case basis, I guess).<br /> <br /> &quot;By Night Studios&quot; (BNS) arouse, from what I gathered, from the LARP community and got the license for LARP rule books, as well as some merchandise, most notably clan symbol pins to wear while larping. They reworked the &quot;Mind's Eye Theatre&quot; (MET) LARP game system and released a new Vampire LARP game. Then they moved on to Werewolf. Martin Ericsson, who was at CCP at the time, supposedly gave them some input on how to change the Setting. When White Wolf was sold from CCP to Paradox, he became the head of Storytelling, therefore seemingly giving some legitimacy to the changes BNS made to the setting.<br /> <br /> While these changes were not in W20, people expected and feared, they might be a glimpse on what WW5th would be like.<br /> Since then Martin Ericsson has left White Wolf and unlike Vampire5th Werewolf 5th will be produced by another company: Hunter Entertainment.<br /> We have little to no idea, what they are up to, and what Paradox-White Wolf is demanding to be incorporated into the Setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 01-19-2021, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-19T14:28:09-08:00","id":1432721,"title":"","content":"Ah, I see. <br /> <br /> What other horrors did he suggest?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-19T15:05:04-08:00","id":1432724,"title":"","content":"Well, we don't know what changes to the Setting stem from him, and what were other authors' ideas and what was feedback from the LARP community.<br /> <br /> The most major change are the destruction of all notable caerns (and septs, I guess) and the Garou nation split into two factions, basically one traditional and one progressive, with the Silent Strider staying neutral. The more progressive faction also became closer to the remaining fera.<br /> From the Gurahl then a Rite was introduced, that allowed to get Caern Shards (from the remaining caerns, I guess) and seed them somewhere appropriate where you wanted to start a new caern. So, that's that.<br /> <br /> I talked to some of the authors during the Grand Masquerade in New Orleans (I think, it wasn't Berlin a year later). And a lot of what I took from this conversations was, that they wanted to make the game more accessible. In WtA W20 and before, Garou and Fera don't mix well. Now, they do. Males, even when feminist, could not be Black Furies, unless metis, now they can. Kinfolk might be viewed by some garou as mere breeding stock (an element of WtA that is hugely misrepresented in the minds of a lot of people, imo), now each kinfolk could be a garou (even more than in W20).<br /> <br /> Also, smaller groups could now have a Caern Shard and the need for a sept was reduced, allowing different play styles with smaller groups in a LARP game. In tabletop there is one pack PCs and everyone else is an NPC. In LARP everyone is an PC in some cases so you need a group that could fill a sept, if not, you have to make adjustments. The new Setting kind of makes that easier, I guess, because smaller groups can now have Caerns/Caern Shards.<br /> <br /> Problem is, that it is an attempt to fix something, that was not broken per s\u00e9.<br /> I mean, if you wanted to play a Bastet instead of a garou, because you like cat but not wolves, then it is your problem. Instead of catering to your needs and changing the whole (game) world for you, you could suck it up and give garou a try or find other people to play a Bastet chronicle with. Sounds harsh and non-inclusive, but besides procrastination roleplaying and larp are means to get out of your comfort zone, do something different and, yes, be and aggressive douch, in case of most garou - the likes of which would not be tolerated in human society unless elected President. Pardon me. No, seriously, Donald, pardon me for all I might do. One pardon more or less won't make a difference, right? Moving on.<br /> <br /> Besides this, there is another thing that I think BNS didn't think through. The traditional faction is denying themselves Weaver's tools of any kind up to fabric. So, can you imagine a werewolf game on the ground of the local college where half the players wear only fur they sewed together themselves? Probably not, but maybe the faction isn't supposed to be played as easily the other one.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there are other differences, and maybe I have remembered something wrong, but that's what I think...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 01-20-2021, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-20T03:32:15-08:00","id":1432769,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> But the whole point of Werewolves were that they're angry and exclusive monsters with heroic qualities... Being Harsh and non-inclusive is kinda <i>The Theme</i>. I felt like I was doing wrong the one time I had a silent strider in my group, nevermind having a mixed-breed game.<br /> We're playing fascistic eco-terrorists<br /> Every tribe is meant to be flawed, The BF excluding men was their flaw. If the biological men at the table want to play black furies, they can play women, or metis. cutting down a tribe's flaw through liberalization just to pander undermines the core themes of the game. The setting is challenging to give you a chance to punch up and, well.... <i>RAGE. </i>It doesn't do well to have your problems solved for you and if anything it's patronizing to have the setting go out of it's way to be so accommodating. I'd see the the Red Talons accept misanthropic homids before I see BF accept feminist men.<br /> <br /> Also the Fera, besides the Corax, are just as much, occasionally more, a problem than the Garou. The Bastet are assholes. The Ajaba are assholes. The Gurahl are assholes. The Rokea are epic-assholes, The Nuwisha are funny assholes, The kitsune are sketchy. The Spiders might as well be aliens. I have no strong opinions on the Mokole. Beyond the Corax the &quot;nice&quot; Fera are all extinct, and even when considering the extinct Fera, most of them are assholes. &quot;Working with the Fera&quot; should only extend to &quot;Not intruding on their territory and trying to kill them&quot; or at most &quot;Using the Raven to take advantage of the Tiger&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the Garou nation split into two factions, basically one traditional and one progressive, </div> </div> </div> ah, the same Democrat/Republican problem that currently plagues current vampire","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 01-20-2021, 06:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-20T07:11:00-08:00","id":1432784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1432769#post1432769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the whole point of Werewolves were that they're angry and exclusive monsters with heroic qualities... Being Harsh and non-inclusive is kinda <i>The Theme</i>. I felt like I was doing wrong the one time I had a silent strider in my group, nevermind having a mixed-breed game.<br /> We're playing fascistic eco-terrorists</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I usually tend to see Garou in a kind of moderate way. They are mostly homid breed so I tend to impose my upper-middle-class, rural upbringing, well educated German personae as a template to them.<br /> So, I see them being non-inclusive about certain people not necessarily as an act of hatred, but a thoughtful decision on there part (as a society). The hostilities now dubbed War of Rage have given way to a cold war like stand between Garou and Fera with suspicion and prejudice on both sides, but no &quot;kill before being killed&quot;-status quo. So, the Fera make good NPCs, are good in Fera-centred games and one of them can even be part of the game, perhaps, but there shouldn't be an alliance or neighbourhood buddy situation, unless one plays Ahadi or Hengeyokai scenarios.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1432769#post1432769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every tribe is meant to be flawed, The BF excluding men was their flaw. If the biological men at the table want to play black furies, they can play women, or metis. cutting down a tribe's flaw through liberalization just to pander undermines the core themes of the game. The setting is challenging to give you a chance to punch up and, well.... <i>RAGE. </i>It doesn't do well to have your problems solved for you and if anything it's patronizing to have the setting go out of it's way to be so accommodating. I'd see the the Red Talons accept misanthropic homids before I see BF accept feminist men.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not sure if every tribe has a flaw, and if that is the Black Fury on, if any.<br /> I think the author, I talked to her specifically, mentioned the reasoning was in part, that the tribe changed policies as a means of survival. How that makes sense I not sure, since the tribe had male kinfolk and was as of revised actively adopting garou of other tribes if they felt not welcome in their own tribe. Meaning any sept would hide away their female cubs and cliaths when a Black Fury comes to visit, for she might repay your hospitality by encouraging your offspring to leave.<br /> <br /> In any case, true, there are some aspects in the game, we today would consider sexist, racist, fascist and so on. Removing or toning them down is in my opinion not helpful for the Setting. Because it doesn't force players to address this issues in the game. Sure, one could say, why should a game, a form of entertainment, do that? But then again, WoD is a storytelling game for a more mature audience then other RPGs are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1432769#post1432769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ah, the same Democrat/Republican problem that currently plagues current vampire</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is not supposed to be played with both factions in the same game, iirc. But, possibly, having a chronicle network with some chronicles favouring the one side, others the other side. Each character also could be on the side he personally favours, being not in the same group as your tribe usually is, is a Merit, iirc. As is being a Fera etc. This stems from the whole idea that you can play everything, if you just bought the necessary Merits. Therefore making it against the rules, basically, to prohibit certain character options in one's game. This is catering to players who want to play but not really play WtA-Garou but WoD-Critters or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-20T10:58:11-08:00","id":1432805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1432769#post1432769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being Harsh and non-inclusive is kinda <i>The Theme</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reactionary, not non-inclusive, though the two can overlap. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Every tribe is meant to be flawed, The BF excluding men was their flaw. </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty big stretch.<br /> <br /> A big problem is that WtA was originally constructed in a very meta fashion with very shallow Tribal cultures. The second the game had to actually expand on things and try to communicate a functional setting for the Garou to inhabit, the one-dimensional original Tribal concepts had to get a lot more nuanced, and a lot things stopped making sense.<br /> <br /> For example, the Black Furies don't get to decide who is and isn't a Black Fury. Pegasus does as their Tribal Totem. So the question is then why doesn't Pegasus allow male gendered non-Metis characters into the Tribe? And there's no actual good reason for it. Pegasus might be pissed off about being gelded, but &quot;man&quot; did that to Pegasus in the sense of humanity not males (even if, yes, a dude did the actual deed). Why would Pegasus hold that against, say, male lupus cubs? Do wolves go around gelding mythological flying horses?<br /> <br /> In any case, once the onus was placed on Pegasus, and not the Tribe itself, it ceased to work as a true flaw for them. It ceased being a &quot;flaw&quot; since the Black Furies couldn't allow men in if they wanted to. It shifts the narrative weight off their shoulders as it's just something they have had to deal with as a subculture for thousands of years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the biological men at the table want to play black furies, they can play women, or metis. cutting down a tribe's flaw through liberalization just to pander undermines the core themes of the game. </div> </div> </div>Or it's just as simple as the setting doesn't actually make coherent sense as written and this was one way to address it. Also it's a game people play to have fun, which isn't always served well by heavy-handed forced narratives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The setting is challenging to give you a chance to punch up and, well.... <i>RAGE. </i>It doesn't do well to have your problems solved for you and if anything it's patronizing to have the setting go out of it's way to be so accommodating. </div> </div> </div>You really thing the BFs no longer excluding men solves their problems for them (in either direction)? The modern feminist movement has included men in it for decades... sexism hasn't magically solved itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1432784#post1432784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the author, I talked to her specifically, mentioned the reasoning was in part, that the tribe changed policies as a means of survival. How that makes sense I not sure, since the tribe had male kinfolk and was as of revised actively adopting garou of other tribes if they felt not welcome in their own tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>The survival math here is actually pretty simple. Male Garou + female Kinfolk is a more efficient breeding pairing than the other way around considering the cultural roles Garou and Kinfolk play in their society. A male Garou can spend a night away from his other duties to get a mate pregnant and leave child rearing to the kin community. A female Garou commits far far more time to the process and thus isn't fighting the Wyrm and all that other stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Removing or toning them down is in my opinion not helpful for the Setting. Because it doesn't force players to address this issues in the game. Sure, one could say, why should a game, a form of entertainment, do that? But then again, WoD is a storytelling game for a more mature audience then other RPGs are. </div> </div> </div>It helps the setting because the setting as is is incoherent.<br /> <br /> It's also not mature to say, &quot;this is the only way to address X topic in our game, screw off if you can't handle it.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-20T13:07:42-08:00","id":1432824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1432805#post1432805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For example, the Black Furies don't get to decide who is and isn't a Black Fury. Pegasus does as their Tribal Totem. So the question is then why doesn't Pegasus allow male gendered non-Metis characters into the Tribe? And there's no actual good reason for it. Pegasus might be pissed off about being gelded, but &quot;man&quot; did that to Pegasus in the sense of humanity not males (even if, yes, a dude did the actual deed). Why would Pegasus hold that against, say, male lupus cubs? Do wolves go around gelding mythological flying horses?<br /> <br /> In any case, once the onus was placed on Pegasus, and not the Tribe itself, it ceased to work as a true flaw for them. It ceased being a &quot;flaw&quot; since the Black Furies couldn't allow men in if they wanted to. It shifts the narrative weight off their shoulders as it's just something they have had to deal with as a subculture for thousands of years.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to derail the thead too much, but I think your conclussions are off given the information provided.<br /> - Male lupus, after the first change, are as human and 'man' as homid men in many senses, and are every bit as capable of cruelty.<br /> <br /> - Spirit logic is not people logic, why are you under the assumption that Pegasus sees gender seperately from sex? And if pegasus does make that distinction, would pegasus be likely to adopt your very human interpretation of should and shouldn't be verboten? Or maybe Pegasus is an all-too-human mercenary neolib spirit who'll allow or ban men based on brand impact... The point being that the the most enlightened and correct viewpoint on gender isn't likely to mean shit to Pegasus, Pegasus is as much an idea as a being.<br /> <br /> - Even if pegasus is the ultimate judge of allowing a man to be a Black Fury, who said the man can even approach the courthouse? Joining a tribe isn't just asking the avatar of an Incarna for a spot, it's a full social process, and the prospective -man- would have to go against both common sense and every woman that's opposed to his joining, never mind the trials that normally happen with initiation rites. If, by some absurd miracle they flip the table and it lands in the right place with all it's dishes unspilt, what happens then? Do you think all the BFs will just take this lying down? Even if Pegasus bothers to vocally support the new pack member, it's unlikely to stop the scorn, career sabotage, accusations of deception... and I'm sure a few more reactionary BFs will attempt murder or at least hound the -man- with duels. Not to mention that those outside the tribe are likely to see this as a massive loss of face for the tribe and question the integrity of the one who caused such an upset... What kind of crazy masochist would do this? Just join one of the other tribes. Those claw gifts are wicked sick, but they're not worth all that shit.<br /> <br /> So yeah, there's plenty of good reasons not to allow -men- in the tribe that doesn't want men.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-20T14:04:45-08:00","id":1432832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1432805#post1432805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, the Black Furies don't get to decide who is and isn't a Black Fury. Pegasus does as their Tribal Totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Pegasus doesn't. Pegasus might have veto power, when it comes to a person entering or leaving the tribe. But, if Pegasus isn't called during a Rite of Passage or Rite of Adoption then there is nothing to veto. At rare occasions a tribal totem might bring someone into to tribe without any Rite or garou participation, but that should be a rare exception.<br /> <br /> Totems are nigh-godlike, but they are not all-knowing, all-seeing or have knowledge of the future. Why would totems take it upon themselves to decide who enters their tribe and who not, bringing them into conflict with one another, when they can leave the decisions to their mortal followers. Tribes are ethnic conglomerates of mortal beings, and they have the power to include someone into their ranks or not - then calling their Totem for approval. The tribes supposedly do so with best knowledge and conscience, and in accordance with old traditions that served them well (or in case of the Uktena, changed their traditions, when the circumstances required it).<br /> <br /> Tribal membership goes like this:<br /> 1. Tribe claims newborn with Baptism of Fire (tribal glyphe on baby, kin-fetch from tribal totem brood.<br /> 2. Tribe educates cub after first change (possible before that, depending on the circumstances and living situation)<br /> 3. If cub is deemed appropriate for tribe, Rite of Passage is celebrated and Tribal Totem is called for approval.<br /> <br /> It does not go like this:<br /> 1. Silverfangs claim newborn with Baptism of Fire (tribal glyphe on baby, kin-fetch from tribal totem brood.<br /> 2. Fianna educate cub after first change, because they don't give a fuck about the Silver Fang glyph and murdered the kin-fetch.<br /> 3. If cub is deemed appropriate for any tribe, Rite of Passage is celebrated and Pegasus claims a cub that has Silver Fang blood and Fianna education, because reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1432805#post1432805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or it's just as simple as the setting doesn't actually make coherent sense as written and this was one way to address it. Also it's a game people play to have fun, which isn't always served well by heavy-handed forced narratives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, it might not make sense how it was written.<br /> One could always try a better explanation or just accept, that Black Furies don't have male in their ranks because of reasons, and move on.<br /> <br /> Sure, people play to have fun. But was there really an outrage so loud, that the fun of male gamers was hindered because they would have to play female character to get &quot;Wasp Talons&quot; and that this would take away their fun? Or was it to prevent cross-dressing during LARPs for it is probably not done well and would lead to slapstick-like or uncomfortable situations? What about the female players, who had fun with the exclusivity of their tribe and are now robbed of it? If they whine to an author of Werewolf 6th Edition about it, will the Get of Fenris finally be an all-girls club?<br /> <br /> Sure, Mark Rein-Hagen didn't build a fully fleshed out world and it was up to others to fill it with substance and the job was not everywhere done well. I get that. But it is okay to stick with some things, even if they are not ideal. So, the Black Furies are like the Electorial College.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1432805#post1432805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The survival math here is actually pretty simple. Male Garou + female Kinfolk is a more efficient breeding pairing than the other way around considering the cultural roles Garou and Kinfolk play in their society. A male Garou can spend a night away from his other duties to get a mate pregnant and leave child carering to the kin community. A female Garou commits far far more time to the process and thus isn't fighting the Wyrm and all that other stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But is that behaviour the Black Furies really would find okay from a man?<br /> <br /> If it was, they could always get garou from other tribes to impregnate their kinfolk and hand them over the kids, if they are male. I think that is what Black Fury kin might have done anyway, when visiting other septs for their Beltaine celebrations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1432805#post1432805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It helps the setting because the setting as is is incoherent.<br /> <br /> It's also not mature to say, &quot;this is the only way to address X topic in our game, screw off if you can't handle it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There are other ways to address exclusive groups in the game, sure. But, this was one of the ways, and it was removed. There had been alternatives to Black Furies to play male garou, and even male metis. For me, it reeks of someone whining long enough till a change was made so he can have something he couldn't have before.<br /> <br /> And, yes, the setting is incoherent, or contradicting, but so is the world.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 01-20-2021, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-20T17:44:11-08:00","id":1432864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1432824#post1432824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Male lupus, after the first change, are as human and 'man' as homid men in many senses, and are every bit as capable of cruelty.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're also just as human and &quot;man&quot; as any homid woman in the same senses. Women are perfectly capable of cruelty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spirit logic is not people logic, why are you under the assumption that Pegasus sees gender seperately from sex? </div> </div> </div>Spirit logic is not people logic is even more reason for Pegasus to not give a shit about what's between someone's legs instead of their dedication to the cause.<br /> <br /> I'm under the assumption that Pegasus sees gender separate from sex because Pegasus was born male and is now a feminine spirit. Pegasus is, by their very nature which is what's most important to spirits, not accepting of bioessentialism. Also Pegasus allows male Metis into the all women Tribe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if pegasus does make that distinction, would pegasus be likely to adopt your very human interpretation of should and shouldn't be verboten? </div> </div> </div>I have no idea what you're referencing with this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or maybe Pegasus is an all-too-human mercenary neolib spirit who'll allow or ban men based on brand impact... The point being that the the most enlightened and correct viewpoint on gender isn't likely to mean shit to Pegasus, Pegasus is as much an idea as a being. </div> </div> </div>I think you might need to study up on ancient and classical Greek mythology and folklore regarding sex and gender.<br /> <br /> Why are you assuming that Pegasus has tossed out thousands of years of interaction with culture to embrace a less-than-200 year old purely human mostly patriarchal and mostly Christian point of view?<br /> <br /> Pegasus doesn't need to be a &quot;mercenary neolib.&quot; Pegasus needs to reflect the Greek mythology that inspired them... which was rather fluid about gender.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if pegasus is the ultimate judge of allowing a man to be a Black Fury, who said the man can even approach the courthouse? </div> </div> </div>The problem with this line of thinking is that it's circular based on the presumption of he Black Furies always been gender-selecting and taking the position of things in the 90s. When the Tribe first formed, before there were generations of culture to create the idea that men shouldn't be allowed to &quot;approach the courthouse,&quot; why didn't any Black Furies want their sons to be given a chance to prove their worth to the Tribe and Pegasus? Why did none of them try? They're not just the &quot;anti-man&quot; Tribe. They're the Tribe that venerates motherhood and wants to raise their children of any body parts to respect egalitarian values. Also there's that whole Ragabash Auspice who have the job of challenging norms and traditions.<br /> <br /> The Tribe isn't a monolith, and once one Black Fury tried to initiate their male child and Pegasus allowed it, it would inherently allow men into the courthouse. The current attitudes of the Tribe don't make any sense unless it has been true for the Tribe's whole history that Pegasus didn't want men in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What kind of crazy masochist would do this? </div> </div> </div>There's a lot of people in the world that subject themselves to all sorts of abusive behavior because of countless reasons. I'm not sure why it's hard to imagine a BF born man in 2020 wanting to fight for his mother, sisters, and aunts as part of Pegasus's Tribe instead of abandoning them for a different Tribe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So yeah, there's plenty of good reasons not to allow -men- in the tribe that doesn't want men. </div> </div> </div>Well, the &quot;Tribe that doesn't want men,&quot; has always had men in it: they're just Metis. There's no actual good reason present for them not to allow; esp. not from the get go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1432832#post1432832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At rare occasions a tribal totem might bring someone into to tribe without any Rite or garou participation, but that should be a rare exception.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;You're all fucking up by taking this to the point of hating men instead of protecting women, so to make it clear, I'm making some of your sons Black Furies in full, get it right,&quot; is certainly a rare exceptional circumstance Pegasus could do.<br /> <br /> [quote]Why would totems take it upon themselves to decide who enters their tribe and who not,...[quote]<br /> <br /> Because it's officially part their job of Tribal Totems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It does not go like this: </div> </div> </div>Depends highly on the Tribal make-up of the Sept. Cubs are raised by the Sept as a communal activity, so multi-Tribe Septs have cubs with teachers from multiple Tribes. It's not the case you're making it to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One could always try a better explanation or just accept, that Black Furies don't have male in their ranks because of reasons, and move on. </div> </div> </div>Or you can make the setting less illogical because making the game better is a good thing instead of just washing your hands of it and moving on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But was there really an outrage... </div> </div> </div>Most of the outrage is around the BFs being presented as rejecting trans women as true women, since it's based in a bioessentialist position that makes no sense for the Black Furies' cultural background or current feminism. Having the Black Furies reject LGBTQ+ minorities as a group they're supposed to protect as part of their mission is a betray of their narrative and in-universe purpose that only serves to alienate minority players. But once you address that... you end up with no reason the Black Furies should actually have ever been anti-penis in their Tribal ranks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What about the female players, who had fun with the exclusivity of their tribe and are now robbed of it? </div> </div> </div>Male Metis BFs mean there was never exclusivity in the first place.<br /> <br /> And IME, female players seeking the BFs as a woman-space are far more put off by men playing BFs to play out male-oriented lesbian erotica than the idea of the Tribe being more inclusive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But it is okay to stick with some things, even if they are not ideal. So, the Black Furies are like the Electorial College. </div> </div> </div>No, some thing need to go. If the BFs are like the Electoral College? They need to be changed ASAP. Especially since we don't need a massive bureaucratic effort to change them. Just the developer and writers to do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But is that behaviour the Black Furies really would find okay from a man? </div> </div> </div>Some of them apparently already are since there are BFs that are stated to treat men as sperm donors and then exclude them from child rearing. Even in less extreme Sept, the BFs are still a matriarchal society and men are expected to respond to the needs of their community rather than dictate their role.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are other ways to address exclusive groups in the game, sure. </div> </div> </div>Camps. Easy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, this was one of the ways, and it was removed. </div> </div> </div>You can't remove something that never was. Again: <b>Male Metis</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, yes, the setting is incoherent, or contradicting, but so is the world. </div> </div> </div>No, the world isn't. It's too complex for us too fully comprehend, so we simplify our perceptions of it, and those perceptions lead to apparent incoherence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T04:44:45-08:00","id":1432902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1432864#post1432864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;You're all fucking up by taking this to the point of hating men instead of protecting women, so to make it clear, I'm making some of your sons Black Furies in full, get it right,&quot; is certainly a rare exceptional circumstance Pegasus could do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, why not.<br /> Pegasus could also make a point and bring in trans-women. All of which are how many percent of the world population and assuming the ratio is identical within the garou Nation leads to how many tans-women garou in total worldwide?<br /> I'd say such an action would qualify as an exception - and I'd be totally fine with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1432864#post1432864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why would totems take it upon themselves to decide who enters their tribe and who not,... </div> </div> </div>Because it's officially part their job of Tribal Totems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page reference?<br /> Revised page 62 mentions that the tribal totem of the tribe initiating the garou approves of the cub's admittance. A passage missing in W20. Key information is, the tribe that initiates the Rite of Passage is mandatory prerequisite for Totem approval. Exceptions are imo possible, but, well, exceptions.<br /> <br /> Obviously, ever since the 1st Edition Rite of Passage source book it is clear, that cubs of various tribes can go in the same quest. It is not clear, however, if only one Ritemaster enacts only one Rite of Passage, mechanically, for all the cubs, therefore circumventing the &quot;the tribe that initiated the Rite&quot; paragraph from revised. Alternatively, this could mean at least one member of each tribe who wants to initiate a cub in a shared quest, would have to perform the Rite of Passage, mechanically.<br /> <br /> W20 explicitly mentions that membership is sometimes expected and not really optional, if you have certain Pure Breed for example. So, depending on the level of peer pressure a cub finds herself under, she or the society decide which tribe she will join and if the Rite of Passage's quest is successful, the tribal totem will approve.<br /> <br /> The book by no means states &quot;the tribal totem choose the tribe of a garou&quot; or &quot;of all the cubs that undergo a Rite of Passage the tribal totems pick their new tribe members&quot;.<br /> <br /> The book also doesn't go into detail, if the tribal totem doesn't approve, for reasons, despite the quest being a success. But that is another story.<br /> <br /> Given the fact that totems aren't all-knowing and have no knowledge of the future, why shouldn't they approve if the quest was successful and worthy. Obviously, there are garou, who later in their career become traitors, cowards, Ronin or BSD. If the Totems would have known before, they might not have admitted them. And there is the Get of Fenris, who later in his career realizes he is actually a Stargazer. Well, Fenris accepted him, right? Or was the author of the 1st Edition TB Stargazer just crazy in his enveloping story?<br /> <br /> Even for mulit-tribal septs it doesn't make sense to enact a &quot;blank&quot; Rite of Passage and see what Totem might accept the cub. This is a level of trying to shift responsibility from the garou who should prepare and educate the cub, to the Totem. Also the core books mention the existance tribal traditions for the Rite of Passage quest in general and some TBs go into detail what this traditions are. &quot;Rite of Passage&quot; also mentions tribal traditions, but it is first edition and cheesy. I mean, if each Black Fury found a lost Caern during her Rite of Passage we would either have Caerns in abundance or would be really bad at remembering where they are...<br /> But, what I'm saying is, the garou would for practical reasons not be able to bring all tribal rite of passage traditions into a &quot;blank&quot; Rite of Passage to make the applicants suitable for each and every tribe.<br /> In the end, the tribal totem is like your bosses boss. You, as Den Parent, do the preparation, determine what tribe the cub is best suited for, prepare the cub, then go to your sept's Master of the Rite to find a suitable quest, date, and all that. Then you bring it before the Moot, maybe, or the Master of Rite and Den Parent have final say according to local sept customs anyway. When the quest starts, this is the time you call your tribal totem, to make it aware of the process. The tribal totem will get his stamp of approval, if nothing is going blatantly wrong. The tribal Totem will not pierce the cubs heart, mind and soul and judge it - at least there is not evidence that it would in the books.<br /> <br /> You don't call all tribal totems just because you can't decide. First time you try, Griffon will rip you to pieces, because the cub was homid and you should have known better. Third time, Fenris will rip you to pieces because you are wasting his time.<br /> <br /> Tribal Totems are the spiritual leaders of the tribes, not their clerks.<br /> If garou are to unsure or indecisive to select a suitable tribe for a cub, then they aren't suited for half of the tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 01-21-2021, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T09:38:30-08:00","id":1432920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1432864#post1432864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're also just as human and &quot;man&quot; as any homid woman in the same senses. Women are perfectly capable of cruelty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe Pegasus bans men because he's jealous of their working cock?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spirit logic is not people logic is even more reason for Pegasus to not give a shit about what's between someone's legs instead of their dedication to the cause.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm under the assumption that Pegasus sees gender separate from sex because Pegasus was born male and is now a feminine spirit. Pegasus is, by their very nature which is what's most important to spirits, not accepting of bioessentialism. Also Pegasus allows male Metis into the all women Tribe. </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This is purely wishful thinking, and you should know it. I'm not trying to disparage your personal views, but your argument here is that you think the spirit is thinking like you do, and thus should take actions according to your line of thought. As Pegasus has not taken action in line with your thought, for thousands of years I might add, either Pegasus doesn't think like you hope, or Pegasus has very little say with what goes on in the tribe, or some combination of the two. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you might need to study up on ancient and classical Greek mythology and folklore regarding sex and gender.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Pegasus doesn't need to be a &quot;mercenary neolib.&quot; Pegasus needs to reflect the Greek mythology that inspired them... which was rather fluid about gender. </div> </div> </div>The Greeks believed children came from sperm, and women were just a convenient holding sacks for gestation. They believed periods were a punishment from the gods, they were absolutely paranoid about women getting involved in politics, and they believed that no respectable person of appropriate age should be on the recieving end of homosexual relations. What ideologically driven, cherry-picking garbage do you have to be reading to think that greek society was fluid about gender?<br /> Now, perhaps if you started with 'Black Furies, like the Get who worship Fenrir, are a counterculture to the greek patriarchy then, yeah, you might've looked like you knew what you were talking about.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Let me throw this one right back at you: Why are you assuming that Pegasus has tossed out thousands of years of interaction with </span></span></span><b>A radical, Rage fueled cult of man-murdering werewolves? </b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem with this line of thinking is that it's circular based on the presumption of he Black Furies always been gender-selecting and taking the position of things in the 90s. When the Tribe first formed, before there were generations of culture to create the idea that men shouldn't be allowed to &quot;approach the courthouse,&quot; why didn't any Black Furies want their sons to be given a chance to prove their worth to the Tribe and Pegasus? Why did none of them try? They're not just the &quot;anti-man&quot; Tribe. They're the Tribe that venerates motherhood and wants to raise their children of any body parts to respect egalitarian values. Also there's that whole Ragabash Auspice who have the job of challenging norms and traditions.<br /> <br /> The Tribe isn't a monolith, and once one Black Fury tried to initiate their male child and Pegasus allowed it, it would inherently allow men into the courthouse. The current attitudes of the Tribe don't make any sense unless it has been true for the Tribe's whole history that Pegasus didn't want men in. </div> </div> </div>Aye, Fenrir should let in weaklings, Shadow lords should let in the kind and stupid, silver fangs should let in the mixed bloods, and Bone Gnawers should start accumulating wealth and get on the property ladder.<br /> Yeah, it's true, for the tribe's whole history pegasus didn't want men in.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, the &quot;Tribe that doesn't want men,&quot; has always had men in it: they're just Metis. There's no actual good reason present for them not to allow; esp. not from the get go. </div> </div> </div>Throughout history, Eunuchs haven't been considered men, and throughout recorded Garou history, Metis have been considered sub-garou. It doesn't take much for one to hold the belief that 'metis aren't men'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because it's officially part their job of Tribal Totems. </div> </div> </div>Totems don't have jobs. They just own stuff. Their properties... I mean the tribes, can figure it out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most of the outrage is around the BFs being presented as rejecting trans women as true women, since it's based in a bioessentialist position that makes no sense for the Black Furies' cultural background or current feminism. Having the Black Furies reject LGBTQ+ minorities as a group they're supposed to protect as part of their mission is a betray of their narrative and in-universe purpose that only serves to alienate minority players. But once you address that... you end up with no reason the Black Furies should actually have ever been anti-penis in their Tribal ranks. </div> </div> </div>So, in short<br /> -You're entirely wrong about the tribe's cultural background.<br /> -Modern femenism isn't the arbiter of a highly traditional tribe who've been around since pre-history. It will have even less of an impact on Pegasus and the associated brood.<br /> -There's plenty reason for the BF to be anti-balls, and you've made the assumption that Pegasus wouldn't be a bio-essentialist because... Pegasus is a spirit and thus really 'spiritual'? Or because you're projecting your own beliefs onto pegasus, or because... What? May I remind you that we're dealing with a gelded winged horse god that stands atop an army badass shapeshifting Rage monsters, not you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And IME, female players seeking the BFs as a woman-space are far more put off by men playing BFs to play out male-oriented lesbian erotica than the idea of the Tribe being more inclusive. </div> </div> </div> Nothing to do with BF. You can do lesbian erotica with anything. You can also do Gay erotica with anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can't remove something that never was. Again: <b>Male Metis</b>. </div> </div> </div> As disgusting as it is, I think they let in male metis because that's how they thought of trans people in the 90's. In any case, male metis makes a poor lynchpin for your argument. If you want to be a trans woman, great; go do that in literally any tribe but the black furies; there are 11 other tribes after all, or bite the bullet and play a metis. If you're a trans woman and want to play a homid BF... just play a woman, there's nothing stopping you. Sexism and shitty behaviour is just part of the setting and I refuse to have the setting go out of it's way to patronize a minority so some writer can inflate themselves with a shallow moral victory at the expense of the setting, which is supposed to be challenging, as a whole. IME my trans players don't play trans characters, they just play their desired gender. The one thing about BF is they're a stickler for gender, and there's nothing in-universe which suggests they should change beyond the ideals of a few pups and claith that don't have the weight to pull anything off. It'd all be out-of-character contrivance or retconning, and people hate that. For me and most I've spoken too, the BF are perfect for what they are, and it'd undermine them and the interesting questions and story possibilities they pose to change that. (especially because, quite frankly, I really, really dislike your personal reinterpretation of the tribe and your alternative view to real history; anything built on lies shouldn't stand)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-21T16:05:37-08:00","id":1432974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1432902#post1432902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, why not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right so, core problem solved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given the fact that totems aren't all-knowing and have no knowledge of the future,... </div> </div> </div>I'm just going to stop you there. When you feel like talking about what I'm actually saying, I'll gladly offer a thoughtful rebuttal. Until then? Take your bad faith strawmen to someone that cares.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tribal Totems are the spiritual leaders of the tribes, not their clerks. </div> </div> </div>And to get back to the <b>actual</b> point:<br /> <br /> The Totems are the spiritual leaders, and thus are the ones responsible for setting things like &quot;you need this much Pure Breed to be a Silver Fang,&quot; or, &quot;You can't be a homid and be a Red Talon,&quot; or, &quot;You can't be a man (sorta) and be a Black Fury.&quot; This undermines the narrative strength of these as cultural positions to be address maturely in the game by having young upstart Garou challenge the oppressive and counterproductive traditions that have failed time and time again in Garou culture: because it's not just a cultural artifact, it's an active rule enforced by literal divine powers that be. There can't be a functional narrative conflict between regressive and progressive factions in Garou society if the regressive factions have the stamp of approval of the Tribal Totems.<br /> <br /> We can't use the game with the setting as is to explore certain topics maturely, because the setting too strongly entrenched certain ideas (presumably under the idea of making them challenging as if they needed help being hard to dislodge) into Garou society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1432920#post1432920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Pegasus bans men because he's jealous of their working cock?</div> </div> </div> </div>Getting hit with the Battle Scar that results in that no longer being the case doesn't let male non-Metis into the Tribe so... nope. Also... I think you're a bit off on what &quot;gelding&quot; means here.<br /> <br /> Of course, why should Pegasus be jealous? You're going very hard at me over ascribing &quot;human&quot; motivations to spirits, but Pegasus can spawn &quot;children&quot; whenever it wants because it's a spirit and they don't reproduce via sex. Pegasus isn't a spirit of jealousy, so there's no reason for Pegasus to have such feelings (except of course as a circular argument to justify the state of the game as-is as acceptable).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is purely wishful thinking, and you should know it. </div> </div> </div>This is a purely bullshit comeback and you should know it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not trying to disparage your personal views,... </div> </div> </div>Try harder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...but your argument here is that you think the spirit is thinking like you do, and thus should take actions according to your line of thought. </div> </div> </div>No I'm not. As I said, Pegasus is literally a spirit that by game canon was born one sex but occupies a gender role associated with women... Pegasus doesn't have to share my personal views, but Pegasus is inherently a spirit that defies bioessentialist thinking. If Pegasus thought being born with a dick meant you couldn't be part of the Black Furies, Pegasus couldn't be part of the Black Furies, let alone male Metis.<br /> <br /> This requires no agreement with my personal beliefs, or anyone else's, just sticking to a cohesive characterization.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As Pegasus has not taken action in line with your thought, for thousands of years I might add, either Pegasus doesn't think like you hope, or Pegasus has very little say with what goes on in the tribe, or some combination of the two. </div> </div> </div>Or, more simply: the world building of the game was done after the Tribes were established the way they were, and this resulted in a large number of inconsistencies in the setting as the writer did their best to dd the history and nuance needed for the game without massive retcons that invalidated the &quot;now&quot; the books were already written in.<br /> <br /> Pegasus's position doesn't make sense because it's the product of a tone of backfilling that was never going to actually create a sensible outcome. The game can either try to move the &quot;now&quot; into a position that helps reduce the impact of that process, or not. W20 Changing Ways was a definite not, BNS WtA was a mixed bag, and who knows what W5 will be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Greeks believed children came from sperm, and women were just a convenient holding sacks for gestation. </div> </div> </div>Um... which Greeks are you talking about? Aristotle (despite being very sexist about it) studied enough biology to recognize that both parents provide &quot;seed&quot; that mixes to form a child. He was even kinda about sperm being necessary to have a male child. His cultural biases were very off on a number of things because of the social value of male heirs, but as far as observations go the surviving body of Greek works on this don't support your claim.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They believed periods were a punishment from the gods,.. </div> </div> </div>Um.. citation needed?<br /> <br /> The Hippocratic school blamed menstruation on women being &quot;spongy&quot; and absorbing more fluid that they then had to purge on a regular basis. Greek rituals around menstruation treated it as a good thing, as they believed it meant the womb had formed properly and it was a sign of fertility, with offerings made specifically to Artemis for healthy and regular periods. Menopause was the &quot;punishment&quot; thing (where men stay fertile but women do not).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...they were absolutely paranoid about women getting involved in politics, and they believed that no respectable person of appropriate age should be on the recieving end of homosexual relations. </div> </div> </div>OK... you know Greek society wasn't just the Athenians, right?<br /> <br /> While most ancient and classical Greek culture were patriarchal, they very wildly in how much political power women could have. Sparta, for all it's obsession about manliness, let women of the proper social class to own land (it was kind of important with such a militaristic cultural to make sure land ownership wasn't thrown into chaos every war), which didn't let them become politicians, but meant they could amass political power much like corporations do today. The Spartan queens in particular were fairly powerful figures in society and the Spartans didn't have a big problem with that.<br /> <br /> The Thebans would also very much disagree with your assertion about sex. The Sacred Band kicked Spartan ass after all, and they were quite proud of that. Half (or more since lots of gay men do both sides of the love making) of their most famous and successful fighting force weren't respectable people? Yeah... no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What ideologically driven, cherry-picking garbage do you have to be reading to think that greek society was fluid about gender? </div> </div> </div>You might go back and note I said &quot;mythology and folklore,&quot; not society as a whole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, perhaps if you started with 'Black Furies, like the Get who worship Fenrir, are a counterculture to the greek patriarchy then, yeah, you might've looked like you knew what you were talking about. </div> </div> </div>If you knew that the Furies in ancient Greece didn't actually have to be &quot;counter-culture&quot; instead of just being defenders of existing cultural elements that were slowly pushed aside as Greece unified and grew less tolerant of certain older practices you might sound like you have any room to judge about who knows what they're talking about.<br /> <br /> This is ultimately when of the most annoying parts about most Internet discussions about the BFs. The BFs were crafted as a counter-culture movement because they're crafted on modern feminism. But linking them back to ancient time doesn't mean their historical inspirations were also counter-cultures. The strange this is that the more accurate-to-history version is more compelling for WtA! The Furies started as part of respected cultural institutions ritualized through deities like Demeter, Artemis, and Athena, but as small villages grew into city-states, and city-states into nations, and nations into an empire, the Weaver's nastier side pushed for the order of patriarchy, leaving the BFs out of their former positions of power, and they've been fighting to reclaim proper balance ever since.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let me throw this one right back at you: Why are you assuming that Pegasus has tossed out thousands of years of interaction with A radical, Rage fueled cult of man-murdering werewolves? </div> </div> </div>Pegasus has never been dealing with &quot;just&quot; a radical Rage fueled cut of man-murdering werewolves. Pegasus has been dealing with a Tribe of werewolves that has had internal factions with a range of views on how to treat men in the fight against patriarchy.<br /> <br /> You're also not reflecting anything back at me here. I'm not &quot;assuming&quot; Pegasus tossed out anything. I'm saying it never made sense for Pegasus to have cared in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Aye, Fenrir should let in weaklings, Shadow lords should let in the kind and stupid, silver fangs should let in the mixed bloods, and Bone Gnawers should start accumulating wealth and get on the property ladder. </div> </div> </div>Or rather, if someone wants to seek membership in with the Fenrir, they should give them a chance to prove it, and if Fenris agrees despite the Fenrir thinking of that applicant as weak, they should suck it up and trust their Totem's judgement that this new Fenrir is bringing strength to the Tribe even if they can't see it for themselves (kinda like they do with Metis already, and how WtA has been in a steady push to stop having the Fenrir treat &quot;women&quot; as &quot;weak&quot; as a generality).<br /> <br /> The Shadow Lords blather is too vague to really deal with.<br /> <br /> The Silver Fangs are barred from letting in anyone with less then PB 3 into the Tribe by Falcon, but that's more of a problem with the way PB works than the concept for the Tribe's purpose in the narrative conflicts of the game. After all House Wyrmfoe, which currently includes the King of the Garou Nation, was originally derided as a &quot;mixed blood&quot; House that included aristocrats, and wealthy families that came out of the Industrial Revolution rather than sticking to old royal blood... and yet still manage to have enough PB to maintain their numbers. The Renewalists have a point because the Silver Fangs have always sought to bring in the ruling class as kinfolk, and getting away from traditional concepts of royal blood to focus on the power of leadership in its new forms is just an extension of what the Tribe has always been about, but the Traditionalists also have a point that capitalist born power is more fleeting than power based in heredity, and they have less struggle with upkeeping PB.<br /> <br /> The Bone Gnawers are, as of W20, free to have as much wealth as they care to get. Status in the Tribe is what you do with it, not if you can get it. The Gnawers care about if you give back, or sell out, not about how much you're worth.<br /> <br /> All you're really doing is seeming to not understand that however cool the 1e shallow concepts for the Tribes sound on paper, actually telling good stories around them requires nuance, not lamentations over half-hearted poorly constructed slippery slopes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, it's true, for the tribe's whole history pegasus didn't want men in. </div> </div> </div>Accept all those men Pegasus let in...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Throughout history, Eunuchs haven't been considered men, and throughout recorded Garou history, Metis have been considered sub-garou. It doesn't take much for one to hold the belief that 'metis aren't men' </div> </div> </div>But if said Metis believe themselves to be men regardless of what contortions the Tribe hypocritically makes to justify the rules they operate under.... the Tribe still lets men in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -You're entirely wrong about the tribe's cultural background. </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Modern femenism isn't the arbiter of a highly traditional tribe who've been around since pre-history. It will have even less of an impact on Pegasus and the associated brood. </div> </div> </div>Yet your entire argument boils down to 18th and 19th century Western views on sex and gender (including biases in historical analysis of ancient culture) as being the arbiter of said Tribe and it's impact on Pegasus. How is that better? Even if your assessment of my position was accurate, at least it was be something relevant to people playing the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -There's plenty reason for the BF to be anti-balls </div> </div> </div>You haven't actually come up with one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...and you've made the assumption that Pegasus wouldn't be a bio-essentialist because... Pegasus is a spirit and thus really 'spiritual'? Or because you're projecting your own beliefs onto pegasus, or because... What? May I remind you that we're dealing with a gelded winged horse god that stands atop an army badass shapeshifting Rage monsters, not you. </div> </div> </div>Addressed above.<br /> <br /> So, in short, your entire argument is simply that the presentation of the BFs needs to be sexist because you seem to firmly be of the position that the ultimate form of punching up is attacking women. Unless you have something less offensive to say in all this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nothing to do with BF. You can do lesbian erotica with anything. You can also do Gay erotica with anything. </div> </div> </div>Deflections are so trite.<br /> <br /> You can do homosexual erotica with anything, yes. But in terms of players and their reactions to the game, the biggest complaint IME regarding men in a &quot;women's&quot; space is male players playing female BFs pushing for women to play lesbians with them. No other Tribe has this particular dynamic because no other Tribe has sex-based membership issues. Men can't try to bully women into playing lesbians with two women Fianna by claiming women are playing Fianna wrong by not being down for some girl-on-girl, as does happen with the Black Furies (yes it's a horrible misrepresentation of the Tribe, but one that's given weight by arguments like the one's your making).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In any case, male metis makes a poor lynchpin for your argument. </div> </div> </div>Not really. Pegasus lets men into the Tribe. The qualifier for why some are and some aren't only undermine any attempt to claim that the BFs are a &quot;women's space&quot; or that they're actually anti-men in the Tribe; such positions are already compromised.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want to be a trans woman, great; go do that in literally any tribe but the black furies </div> </div> </div>And this is the fundamentally sexist/transphobic part of your argument. &quot;Hey black people, why eat where white people want to eat without you, you can go eat with other black people, or white that want to mix with you,&quot; is not an argument anyone that doesn't want to get called a racist would make. The themes and causes of the Black Furies are themes and causes are going to appeal to LGBTQ+ players and characters. If you want to play a trans woman WtA PC, your Tribe should be selected based on your character's relationships to those elements, not some bullshit bioessentialism that adds nothing to the game. No Tribe should be off-limits to trans characters, because anyone that wants to explore how the Tribe's themes interplay with a trans character should be free to do so. Nobody's forcing you to do that in your game, but you're advocating keeping the books in a state that tells other people not to play in a way you don't seem to care for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sexism and shitty behaviour is just part of the setting and I refuse to have the setting go out of it's way to patronize a minority so some writer can inflate themselves with a shallow moral victory at the expense of the setting, which is supposed to be challenging, as a whole. </div> </div> </div>You do realize you're doing nothing but being patronizing to inflate your shallow moral self-satisfaction in defense of a setting that only exists as a function of a game, right?<br /> <br /> Sexism in the setting doesn't disappear if the BFs are more inclusive. There's still all the shitty sexism in Garou society and human society to deal with. Changing the Tribes to be less cringeworthy and more nuanced isn't at the expense of the setting, it's for the improvement of the setting so you can tell good stories about the challenges of combating sexism by having a stronger foundation to build off of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> IME my trans players don't play trans characters, they just play their desired gender. </div> </div> </div>Every trans and NB player I have ever played with has done both. IME, they play more trans and NB characters the more safe they feel with the cis players in the group. They play more cis characters when they're worried about having to deal with cis players that they don't feel will respect trans character play.<br /> <br /> So... maybe consider that the trans players in your group aren't sending you the signal you think they are. Maybe they are! But if you talk to a wider group of LGBTQ+ people, you'll find that this sort of code-switching behavior is the norm, not the exception.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The one thing about BF is they're a stickler for gender,... </div> </div> </div>Except when they're not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It'd all be out-of-character contrivance or retconning, and people hate that. </div> </div> </div>WtA's history is one long series of retcons. People's reactions to said retcons are based in execution more than not; though of course allowing for the gorgnards that consider any change bad.<br /> <br /> If the end result is a better game, then people generally adapt just fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> especially because, quite frankly, I really, really dislike your personal reinterpretation of the tribe and your alternative view to real history; anything built on lies shouldn't stand </div> </div> </div>Wow... &quot;we disagree on this thing, I don't like your version, therefore your version is a lie and morally reprehensible!&quot;<br /> <br /> If that's the argumentation you're going to go with? Please retract all your posts, on this topic because they shouldn't stand on their foundations of lies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 01-21-2021, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T01:19:05-08:00","id":1433024,"title":"","content":"Right, yeah, I suppose the Greeks before the archaic period were better towards women. Pitty such little writing exists for them... Can you find a source to suggest they were genderfluid? And if they were accepting of other genders can you also ascertain that a transwoman would be fully accepted as a woman, because what I'm reading(of later periods) would suggest that transmen still couldn't get into politics, even in those less sexist cities like Sparta. I'd love to be proven wrong and find some concrete proof of minoans being very liberal with gender, but nobody can read linear B, and I'm weary from all those -Ancient greeks were super gay, just like modern people- bullshit that people like to espouse. <br /> (also you know believing in something from a far earlier time still makes you a counterculture? even if your history is legitimate the present is what defines a counterculture.) <br /> <br /> <br /> The Black Furies have consistently been portrayed as characters who'll claw through ten men to save a woman, before even considering the scenario. What makes you think they got the time or the incentive to care about trans women? You know werewolf tribes double as cults right? A lot of very real LGB groups want to &quot;drop the T&quot; after all. Allowing Trans characters to join the BF wouldn't get more than a handful of members worldwide, while it'd upset the huge chunk of more conservative members; not really worth it, from a purely in-universe view. <br /> <br /> Also, where can I find out about Pegasus being a She that defies bioessentialist thinking? Is there a book? Is it one of those really recent 20th books written by freelancers? <br /> Is it really so much for a tribe to be flawed? Must they be the perfect pro-women group of werewolves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T03:00:41-08:00","id":1433029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433024#post1433024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, yeah, I suppose the Greeks before the archaic period were better towards women.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Better&quot; is relative, but the more important thing is that prior to the Macedonian conquering of Greece and the start of the Hellenistic period there wasn't a single &quot;Greek&quot; culture or society, but a bunch of them with lots of different attitudes (that were hardly static over centuries) and any general claims about their society are bound to run afoul of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you find a source to suggest they were genderfluid? </div> </div> </div>Is there a particular reason you want me to find a source for a claim I didn't make?<br /> <br /> There is a big difference between what the Greeks enacted as social norms, and what they considered valid things deities and other mythological creature were capable of doing or being. I'm talking about Pegasus as a mythological figure, not the rights different Greek city-states granted to people that chose to live social roles associated with a different sex from their birth. So... I really don't get why you're continuing to bang on about the rest of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Black Furies have consistently been portrayed as characters who'll claw through ten men to save a woman, before even considering the scenario. </div> </div> </div>They've been consistently stereotyped as this, which isn't the same thing as being consistently portrayed as this. The Amazons of Diana are the most visible Camp within the Tribe, and frequently act like that, but most Black Furies look down on such behavior (esp. their primary rivals for being the dominate Camp by numbers in the Bacchantes who are just as deadly but far more thoughtful and deliberate in their actions). Mari Cabrah, one of the major canon NPCs who we get to see in action is highly dismissive of the Amazons and the reputation they've given the Tribe. She (and she's an Elder ranked Garou, so she has significant sway on top of being Jonas's packmate) has one of the simplest counter-points in existence: she runs self defense classes so women and learn to stand up for themselves rather than letting women get abused and then avenging the crime. Mari is hardly restrained if she sees abuse in action, but she's repeatedly shown as being closer to the Baccantes in actually taking stock of the situation before acting; though it doesn't hurt that as a Theurge she's more open to alternatives than just attacking.<br /> <br /> To quote W20:<br /> <br /> &quot;The tribe holds that women are worthy of respect, honor, sometimes even veneration. Though no Black Fury will suffer the hand of a man acting as master or tyrant, the tribe isn\u2019t united by active misandry. Certainly some Furies will never forget or forgive. But others are willing to accept men as partners, helpmates, lovers, equals \u2014 but nothing more than equals. Lupus Furies have less of an immediate connection to the hardships of human women, as female wolves have no real discrimination to bear, but they are deeply tied to the Wyld and learn great empathy for their human and homid sisters.<br /> <br /> Hatred claims the hearts of many Furies, but it\u2019s not a tribal virtue. The true tribal virtues are honor, pride, the mysticism of the Wyld, and the will to exact change. A Fury aspires to keep her word, to stand tall rather than bend a knee, to guard and exult in the wildest places, and to fight until her dying breath to make the world a better place.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's how the books present what the Furies truly are, rather than the stereotypes brought on by their more brash and Ragey members.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What makes you think they got the time or the incentive to care about trans women? </div> </div> </div>Because it's part of their mission to make the world a better place which, in their view, includes supporting those oppressed by patriarchy. As they consider the spiritual embodiment of patriarchy as their primary foe (to an extent more than the Wyrm because they see the Patriarch as one of the Wyrm's most effective agents despite him technically being a Weaver spirit), anything that is a knock against the patriarchy is them fulfilling their divinely mandated role. Caring about trans rights is fighting the patriarchy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You know werewolf tribes double as cults right? </div> </div> </div>Yes. And in this case a cult has an active group within it that seeks to use modern new age spirituality to encourage men to get in touch with their feminine side as a method of converting them to their cult's veneration of Gaia and Luna as female deities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A lot of very real LGB groups want to &quot;drop the T&quot; after all. </div> </div> </div>No, a lot of TERFs are loud on the Internet and try to hid their transphobia behind letters that make them sound like they care about LGB rights (which they don't if they exclude LGB trans people!). Jared Kushner might be Jewish, but he's done jack shit for actual Jewish advocacy groups in the US, and giving money to a Jewish sounding group like AIPAC doesn't change that. Groups can call themselves whatever they want. What they do matters.<br /> <br /> Actual LGB activists embrace the trans and NB communities because there wouldn't be a modern LGB movement without it being a LGBTQ+ movement. The acknowledgement that their an alliance of people all fighting for the same cause is what gives them power against the majority that they wouldn't have separately.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say that alliance is going perfectly, but it's less about LG folks not actually believing in BTQ+ rights, but the ugly human tendency to duck out of the social fight once you get yours even if the people that fought to get that for you still haven't gotten theirs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Allowing Trans characters to join the BF wouldn't get more than a handful of members worldwide, while it'd upset the huge chunk of more conservative members; not really worth it, from a purely in-universe view. </div> </div> </div>The Garou are a dying race (as of W20 at least) and every member counts; if the Black Furies are desperate enough to poach members of other Tribes' cubs... some of them are certainly going to be open to the idea of not being TERFs. And doing the right thing even if it pisses off the hidebound members of the Tribe is a central theme of WtA and thus something that game needs to facilitate being possible. Every Tribe has internal conflicts around this as it is (though some a bit less than others). Making it clear that trans women Garou can be Black Furies mechanically, means that struggle is actually valid to do in the game; saying it's mechanically impossible denies an expression of one of the game's central conflicts.<br /> <br /> [quote]Also, where can I find out about Pegasus being a She that defies bioessentialist thinking?[/quote[<br /> <br /> You might notice that I, like the books, refer to Pegasus in gender neutral terms. Becoming they instead of she is just as much a rejection of bioessentialism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is it really so much for a tribe to be flawed? Must they be the perfect pro-women group of werewolves? </div> </div> </div>Is it really so hard for you to see that the Tribe would still be massively flawed anyway? Getting rid of a pointlessly off-putting aspect of the Tribe doesn't magically make them perfect.<br /> <br /> Getting rid of the &quot;Silver Fangs are all inbred because the only way to imagine modern royals is the Habsburgs even though most royals around the globe didn't have that problem,&quot; didn't make the Silver Fangs the perfect Tribe of Royalty. Turning the neo-Nazi stuff in the Fenrir from a prominent part of the Tribe into a Camp they internally wiped out didn't make them the perfect Tribe of Strength.<br /> <br /> If this is the only flaw you can find in the Tribe such that fixing it would make the Furies perfect? Maybe go reread some of the books because they have so many flaws; and frankly much more interesting ones than getting into generational feminist infighting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T04:38:38-08:00","id":1433037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pegasus doesn't need to be a &quot;mercenary neolib.&quot; Pegasus needs to reflect the Greek mythology that inspired them... which was rather fluid about gender. </div> </div> </div>You did write this, but Ok, yeah, point taken; the myths and the society that manufactured them don't equate. I mean, Loki was trans, and everybody hated him for it. <br /> <br /> Look, for me at least, part of the enjoyment from werewolf is the Rage, the cathartic, eternal fight against a world filled with injustices. The more challenging and uphill the battle, the better. Lots of people want happy resolutions to such settings, but applying them robs the setting of it's conflict and intrigue. People enjoy challenge, and tribes are meant to be exclusive, not inclusive. Werewolves are elitists (The Bone Gnawers engage in more than a fair bit of reverse snobbery). The more exclusive each tribe, the stronger their themes and the more to rage against. And I quite like fostering inter-tribal rivalry so characters who resent the BF for not letting 'her' join are great (but also... most folks will generally change and join a tribe before they realise they're trans?).<br /> <br /> <br /> In context with everything else, I just find the prospect of BF accepting Trans women patronizing. Do trans women really need to be so coddled? If it's really -pegasus just sees the inner gender rather than the outer sex- then do they bar trans-men from joining in that case? I don't see a readily believable in-universe explanation for why the Black Furies would go without men (metis excluded) for thousands of years and suddenly change when the trans movement has some amount of traction... no thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-22T12:22:53-08:00","id":1433085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433037#post1433037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>Do trans women really need to be so coddled?</b></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">No, but apparently you do. Take a month off and maybe try reading the forum rules about post civility, personal attacks, and hate speech. </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-24T16:36:56-08:00","id":1433328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1432974#post1432974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Totems are the spiritual leaders, and thus are the ones responsible for setting things like &quot;you need this much Pure Breed to be a Silver Fang,&quot; or, &quot;You can't be a homid and be a Red Talon,&quot; or, &quot;You can't be a man (sorta) and be a Black Fury.&quot; This undermines the narrative strength of these as cultural positions to be address maturely in the game by having young upstart Garou challenge the oppressive and counterproductive traditions that have failed time and time again in Garou culture: because it's not just a cultural artifact, it's an active rule enforced by literal divine powers that be. There can't be a functional narrative conflict between regressive and progressive factions in Garou society if the regressive factions have the stamp of approval of the Tribal Totems.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it is your position that these positions originated with the tribal totems. There is not actual text reference that falcon ever mandated Pure Breed or Pegasus is solely responsible for exclusion of males, as opposed to a practice that developed in this tribe on its own.<br /> <br /> The rules are also not enforced by divine power within the game world, for lack of text reference to that, but are enforced by the game mechanics. They don't state the Totems enforce these restrictions the rules present. On the contrary the rules explicitly state, as I quoted above, that garou society does limit the tribal choices of a cub from the moment they prepare them for RIte of Passage.<br /> <br /> Changing the rules and the Setting in this regard doesn't allow progressive factions to function as progressive factions at all, for you can't fight for men within the Black Furies, for the rules now allow them.<br /> <br /> Instead of changing the tribe one should have created an option to address the matter and possibly give players a scenario to affect change within the tribe for there game if they wanted to, but still maintain the original state for those who don't want the change - or don't want the change dictated to them by a game designer.<br /> <br /> <br /> We can't use the game with the setting as is to explore certain topics maturely, because the setting too strongly entrenched certain ideas (presumably under the idea of making them challenging as if they needed help being hard to dislodge) into Garou society.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the matter of trans-women and the Black Furies position towards them, I think that the tribe should and would include MtF-Transgender people. I'd also believe that a fictional FtM-Transgender person would/should leave the tribe behind. That said, I would also think that the tribe would welcome non-binary or asexual people, who are biologically female as well as garou born with male-and-female primary sex organs.<br /> That said, I find it okay that these issues are addressed within the rules, although they only are relevant for a minority group. If the ratio of transgender people in the human population is equal to those of the homid garou population (and why shouldn't it be) then within the whole garou nation there are rally few individual garou present who are actually transgender. There wouldn't be a need to change the Black Fury tribe just to address that, especially since there Glass Walkers, Children of Gaia and several other tribes would also have them (and are probably the tribes the garou would take up anyway, for being transgender isn't these garous only charakter quality, so they would still have more than that to match between tribal philosophy and their personality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 01-24-2021, 07:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-24T17:20:40-08:00","id":1433331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433328#post1433328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it is your position that these positions originated with the tribal totems. There is not actual text reference that falcon ever mandated Pure Breed or Pegasus is solely responsible for exclusion of males, as opposed to a practice that developed in this tribe on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>W20: &quot;Pegasus, their tribal totem, will not accept male Garou.&quot;<br /> <br /> What was that about no text reference?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changing the rules and the Setting in this regard doesn't allow progressive factions to function as progressive factions at all, for you can't fight for men within the Black Furies, for the rules now allow them. </div> </div> </div>Progress isn't a binary. Reforming the Black Fury attitudes towards men (though compare my quote last page to 1e's blurb about them some time) enough to hit one milestone doesn't mean the job is done.<br /> <br /> The US finally electing a black president, and a black/south east Asian vice president didn't end racism in the US, even if those are major milestones for progress towards those goals.<br /> <br /> But you currently can't reform the Black Furies because the rules don't allow a way to change things.<br /> <br /> I seriously do not understand this whole attitude of, &quot;if you make this one thing more progressive, all conflict in the setting is over, the WoD is now the World of Sunshine and Sparkles, and nothing bad is ever going to happen now.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Instead of changing the tribe one should have created an option to address the matter and possibly give players a scenario to affect change within the tribe for there game if they wanted to, but still maintain the original state for those who don't want the change - or don't want the change dictated to them by a game designer. </div> </div> </div>1) Creating an option to &quot;address the matter and possibly give players a scenario to affect change,&quot; <b>is changing the Tribe</b>.<br /> <br /> 2) Plenty of changes are for the better, and worried about people that don't want to be dictated too, means letting a bad thing stand to satisfy the feelings of a few. The designers &quot;dictated&quot; that the Fenrir would no longer be protagonists that actively support neo-Nazis rather than having neo-Nazi Fenrir being something that players hand expunge from the setting if they feel like; no matter how many groups either banned Fenrir or skipped the game completely for having neo-Nazis as good guys.<br /> <br /> Oddly enough, Pegasus, when acting as a pack Totem, accepts all members that fight for women, even while Pegasus would disallow some of those pack members into the Tribe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ....so they would still have more than that to match between tribal philosophy and their personality. </div> </div> </div>And again, the idea that the Black Furies should reject people that perfectly match their philosophy because of body parts doesn't really make sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-24T21:40:55-08:00","id":1433357,"title":"","content":"I believe the limitations of tribal acceptance of certain new members is something that is due to both tribal culture separate from the totem and the totem itself.<br /> <br /> Many years ago when I first joined the forum, I <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/624930-silver-fangs-and-minimum-pure-breed\">asked this</a> specifically in regards to Silver Fangs and the need for Pure Breed 3. There wasn't any consensus. So it comes to ST fiat based on what they feel is correct given the situation.<br /> <br /> We know that Griffin simply doesn't accept any homids - period. Not in the tribe and not in the pack. And we get other spirits as pack totems that also reject homids as members. This is clearly something to do with the spirit. We also know that spirits have certain taboos that they cannot violate, or they weaken and fall into slumber. Likely, such bans are related to such things. The spirits in question simply can't be the patron of certain Garou because it somehow violates their very nature.<br /> <br /> We also know that some discriminating tribes reject candidates out of hand. Stargazers simply won't accept Garou who can't handle certain philosophical inquiries They require a certain level of intelligence/wisdom and interest in such questions. The Get of Fenris don't accept weaklings - their preparation of cubs even leads to death sometimes, and the tribe is find with it as it winnows out the unworthy. At the same time, is there really <i>just</i> a case of the tribal culture, and the totems in question would accept people who are weak in mind or body? I would say no. Chimera just won't accept someone who can't figure out certain problems that require Enigmas. Fenris won't accept physical weaklings. The tribes developed these challenges because they know what their tribal totem's expectations are - and in fact may have witnessed the displeasure of their tribal totem at one point at being presented with unworthy candidates for acceptance into the tribe. This doesn't mean the tribe's selection criteria is perfect - they might cut off candidates who could be acceptable. And they might allow candidates in that fail and anger the totem. But it works well enough in general that the totem is satisfied.<br /> <br /> Even the Fianna have certain criteria for their members, and they aren't known as a particularly discriminating tribe. They still expect candidates to display certain mastery of skills before they become members. But this may just be cultural, and not something Stag is particularly concerned with (other than as a totem of Respect, he has certain expectations that tribe members present a good image). In this case, slipshod septs might allow members in that violate minimal standards, but the tribe likely acts against such septs before it becomes too much of a problem.<br /> <br /> Then we have weird things like the Wendigo not accepting candidates who aren't indigenous American Indians. This was even mirrored in the pack totem's ban to help indigenous people's. This seems to have fairly weak IC/setting justification, but was probably included simply because the original designers wanted a tribe exclusively based on Indians as a hook. But there isn't anything obvious about a spirit of terrible winters, and hunger driving people into cannibalism to be &quot;native only.&quot; Other than the ridiculous pack totem ban (which I never liked), this clearly seems to be a case of tribal culture. And White Wolf immediately subverted that requirement in second edition corebook when they introduced Evan Heals the Past. Now there may be some justification for this, like somehow members of the Wendigo must be ancestrally linked to one of the original Wendigo tribe members so many thousands of years ago. It could have been part of reciprocal chiminage. But I don't believe any justification was ever developed in the books (though I could be wrong, please enlighten me if so).<br /> <br /> So there's a spectrum. Every gaming group will come to its conclusions as to where &quot;this&quot; case lies on that spectrum.<br /> <br /> But if it is possible for Group X, that was previously forbidden to be in the tribe, to become members now, we should ask ourselves why there weren't in previous years? Why haven't we heard about that Silver Fang father who illegally used a rite to make his Pure Breed 2 Garou son into a Silver Fang? Why weren't we told about those Anatolian eunuchs worshipping Cybele that became Black Furies? Were there such cases, but simply hushed up? Or is the evidence of absence in previous books evidence that such things never happened. Or it is only now that such special snowflake style things happen?<br /> <br /> No doubt we might see stuff like this in future material. But let's ignore that this is just a retcon, and does not reflect what the game originally stated. That's not necessarily a deal breaker for an individual gaming group. There are all sorts of stuff I find stupid in canon and ignore in the games I run. I may think this makes for a better game. But I don't pretend its canon.<br /> <br /> I think retcons needlessly divide the fanbase and creates all sorts of other problems. We don't need official rulings to comfort a particular group of the fanbase by rejecting existing lore. Just keep silent and allow each individual ST determine what is true in their games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-24T22:33:26-08:00","id":1433361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433357#post1433357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there's a spectrum. Every gaming group will come to its conclusions as to where &quot;this&quot; case lies on that spectrum.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Black Fury/Pegasus thing falls squarely in the &quot;Totem says no,&quot; part of things. It's clearly stated in the books where it falls on the spectrum. It's not the Wendigo with Evan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think retcons needlessly divide the fanbase and creates all sorts of other problems. We don't need official rulings to comfort a particular group of the fanbase by rejecting existing lore. </div> </div> </div>Who's complaining about retconning out the neo-Nazi Get of Fenris? How is that dividing the fanbase? Why is it a bad thing that we have an official ruling that &quot;comforts&quot; the particular group of, &quot;we don't want neo-Nazis as good guys in our game,&quot; just because it alters existing lore?<br /> <br /> The lore of the game isn't sacred. It's a tool. If your tool is broken, and you can fix it, you fix it. Any emotional attached you had to that tool is easily replaced by emotional attachments to the better version of it after it's fixed. It's been done lots of time already in WtA's history. Rarely has it actually been divisive. In fact usually it removes divisive things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just keep silent and allow each individual ST determine what is true in their games. </div> </div> </div>Or don't, because silence is not always the right response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T02:06:42-08:00","id":1433373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433331#post1433331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">W20: &quot;Pegasus, their tribal totem, will not accept male Garou.&quot;<br /> <br /> What was that about no text reference?</div> </div> </div> </div>Touch\u00e9.<br /> W20 page 48: The Black Furies, for example, accept only female Garou.<br /> W20 page 80: Pegasus, their tribal totem, will not accept male Garou.<br /> <br /> So, which is it? Any references besides the Corebook of half-baked Setting changes?<br /> I did full text searches with various key words through revised and both TB and didn't find that the ban of males was solely Pegasus' idea. Basically, if tribal culture doesn't allow for males, why should Pegasus admit them (unless the ST wants to run a story about that theme) and vice versa Black Furies won't bring male garou before Pegasus with a Rite of Passage because they won't be accepted. While both statements are true, none states the ban originated from either party solely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433331#post1433331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Progress isn't a binary. Reforming the Black Fury attitudes towards men (though compare my quote last page to 1e's blurb about them some time) enough to hit one milestone doesn't mean the job is done.<br /> <br /> The US finally electing a black president, and a black/south east Asian vice president didn't end racism in the US, even if those are major milestones for progress towards those goals.<br /> <br /> But you currently can't reform the Black Furies because the rules don't allow a way to change things.<br /> <br /> I seriously do not understand this whole attitude of, &quot;if you make this one thing more progressive, all conflict in the setting is over, the WoD is now the World of Sunshine and Sparkles, and nothing bad is ever going to happen now.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You make it sound as if the Black Furies opening up to males is a goal that need to be achieved like the end of racism based inequalities in the general public. But it isn't.<br /> Male garou are only banned from the Black Furies based on gender, not from the whole Garou Nation, nor do they suffer hardships due to gender within the garou nation.<br /> The Black Furies are a minority group who have this restriction towards joining their group. Having the authors change the setting in this regard is a false interpretation of political correctness. For any society to be just, there needs to be the freedom to form groups that only includes some people. It is a fundamental right and personal freedom to do so, as long as it doesn't unjustly harm the freedoms of another.<br /> <br /> So, by the editorial decision to open the tribe to males, they robbed the Black Furies of a right, by giving the right to join the tribe to the males without any need, for they weren't unjustly hindered in their lives by not being able to join the Black Furies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433331#post1433331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Creating an option to &quot;address the matter and possibly give players a scenario to affect change,&quot; <b>is changing the Tribe</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it is a clear statement and story hook to an ST and the troupe that the tribe could be different, but isn't in the general setting. Allowing the situation to change from the established Setting, if the troupe feels more comfortable with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433331#post1433331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Plenty of changes are for the better, and worried about people that don't want to be dictated too, means letting a bad thing stand to satisfy the feelings of a few. The designers &quot;dictated&quot; that the Fenrir would no longer be protagonists that actively support neo-Nazis rather than having neo-Nazi Fenrir being something that players hand expunge from the setting if they feel like; no matter how many groups either banned Fenrir or skipped the game completely for having neo-Nazis as good guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, interesting topic. Several European governments have moved towards right-wing nationalism and in Germany we have the rise of a right-wing party. This leads to question of how to deal with them. Just ignoring them or denying them legitimacy seems to be inviting disaster.<br /> So, changing the Setting is kind of not dealing with the problem. In fact there might very well be more people the Secret Service counts as neo-Nazis in Germany, than there are transgender people.<br /> <br /> I wonder why if anybody skipped the game because of some garou seeing their kinfolk as breeding stock. For this is a quote often given, not really the truth for a majority of the garou nation. Still, the problem was attempted to be fixed by making kinfolk undistinguishable from pre-change garou and giving them even broader access to magic. If only we could solve our real world problems by altering reality with a new edition instead of addressing them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433331#post1433331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oddly enough, Pegasus, when acting as a pack Totem, accepts all members that fight for women, even while Pegasus would disallow some of those pack members into the Tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because Pegasus can accept males who fight for the young and the females, but knows that there are females who need a social group free of males and therefore provides them with his tribe as a place to live within.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433331#post1433331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And again, the idea that the Black Furies should reject people that perfectly match their philosophy because of body parts doesn't really make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to make sense. There are feelings involved. Social stigmata. Sense of companionship and kinship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T04:27:15-08:00","id":1433380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433373#post1433373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Touch\u00e9.So, which is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Both, since they're not mutually exclusive. The issue is that Pegasus is one that changes it from just a Tribal cultural value, to being a spiritual rule for the Tribe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any references besides the Corebook of half-baked Setting changes? </div> </div> </div>What's the point? You've made it clear that you'll just label anything else found as bad/wrong/mistaken/etc. by the authors. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You make it sound as if the Black Furies opening up to males is a goal that need to be achieved like the end of racism based inequalities in the general public. But it isn't. </div> </div> </div>Ending systemic sexism isn't going to happen if you cling to second wave feminism techniques. Those are fine for combating overt and direct sexism, but if the Tribe's goal is to make the world a better place, they're going to eventually have to move their ideology forward as well.<br /> <br /> You can't defeat the Patriarch spreading toxic masculinity with exclusionary feminism. It's not a matter of bad men do or don't have it in the rest of the Nation. It's a matter of being able to engage in the communities you want to improve. Enforcing the idea that the only way to join the Tribe that focuses on defending women and children, is to embrace TERFy beliefs, just argues that TERFs are right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For any society to be just, there needs to be the freedom to form groups that only includes some people. </div> </div> </div>That doesn't mean organizations on the scale of Tribes are actually well served by being said groups (and the Garou have other options besides Tribes to create spaces for specific minorities).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, by the editorial decision to open the tribe to males, they robbed the Black Furies of a right,... </div> </div> </div>The Black Furies can still have women's only spaces if they want them. They already have to do that with sub-groups within the Tribe because, again, the Tribe has men in it already. No &quot;rights&quot; have been robbed from them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, it is a clear statement and story hook to an ST and the troupe that the tribe could be different, but isn't in the general setting. Allowing the situation to change from the established Setting, if the troupe feels more comfortable with that. </div> </div> </div>In this specific case, it can only exist if you also change the Tribe-as-written.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, interesting topic. Several European governments have moved towards right-wing nationalism and in Germany we have the rise of a right-wing party. This leads to question of how to deal with them. Just ignoring them or denying them legitimacy seems to be inviting disaster. </div> </div> </div>Deplatforming them actually does wonders. But beyond that? Don't make them heroes in fiction seems like a no-brainer to me.<br /> <br /> If you were in charge of writing an RPG aimed at a German audience, and you don't like the rise of right-wing fascists, do you:<br /> <br /> A) Make sure to include more sympathetic representations of said political beliefs so people that have them feel reaffirmed that you believe their beliefs are good?<br /> or<br /> B) Make sure to depict such beliefs as dangerous and intolerable to a just society, hoping that some might see that it's a bad idea to go down that road, or at least you don't have to worry about about anyone else thinking you're encouraging them with your game?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wonder why if anybody skipped the game because of some garou seeing their kinfolk as breeding stock. </div> </div> </div>I know people that avoid the game because they find the Kinfolk angle distasteful, yes. Lots of people know what it's like to live like a second class citizen even if the first class citizens mean well and don't generally treat you like shit. WtA doesn't really explore it well to make it compelling to use it to explore that for some people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still, the problem was attempted to be fixed by making kinfolk undistinguishable from pre-change garou and giving them even broader access to magic. </div> </div> </div>1) One Gift not being able to tell the difference doesn't mean the game was changed to make it so nothing can.<br /> <br /> 2) I've never seen any statement that's why the change to that Gift was made.<br /> <br /> 3) They have the exact same access to magic they had all the way back in the first Kinfolk book from '97 (that is, a late 2e book), and were always implied to have broad access to magic (long before Unsung Heroes, there were kin that were also supernaturals like mages and changelings).<br /> <br /> The only thing that KABA really did, and I don't see how it's a bad thing, was dedicate more space to what &quot;good&quot; kinfolk life is like, rather than what it isn't. It's a fairly important thing when setting the tone of prose. If you talk about the negatives, even if only as exceptions, they are what stick in people's minds. You need to talk about the positives as well so people treat the positives as the default.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, because Pegasus can accept males who fight for the young and the females, but knows that there are females who need a social group free of males and therefore provides them with his tribe as a place to live within. </div> </div> </div>And then lets males in anyway. Again. The &quot;Metis males are allowed in,&quot; kills any claim to the Black Furies as a women's only social group; since they're not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It doesn't have to make sense. There are feelings involved. Social stigmata. Sense of companionship and kinship. </div> </div> </div>It doesn't have to be strictly rational... it still has to make sense on an emotional level.<br /> <br /> Have you actually be part of a minority rights activist group? Esp. as someone that's not part of that minority? <br /> <br /> The Black Furies aren't what those groups actually look like. Not now, not 60 years ago. Not 100 years ago. Not even longer. They're always coalition groups. Yes, the minority is in the center, and in the lead (at least if there's any chance of success historically speaking). Yes they want spaces where even the best allies don't need to be asked to not enter. But they always look for those allies. They bring those allies into the fold. That's part of reducing social stigma: companionship and kinship with people one step removed (and hopefully more as the movement grows). People they can trust and rely on. Those alliances aren't just social power, they're community, love, and friendship too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T08:20:00-08:00","id":1433393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433380#post1433380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't defeat the Patriarch spreading toxic masculinity with exclusionary feminism. It's not a matter of bad men do or don't have it in the rest of the Nation. It's a matter of being able to engage in the communities you want to improve. Enforcing the idea that the only way to join the Tribe that focuses on defending women and children, is to embrace TERFy beliefs, just argues that TERFs are right.</div> </div> </div> </div>TERF are <b>trans-exclusionary radical feminist</b> according to wikipedia. Doesn't really apply to my argument, though. For as I wrote, Pegasus and the tribe should make exceptions for transgender people. They should imo not open their tribe to males in general, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433380#post1433380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't mean organizations on the scale of Tribes are actually well served by being said groups (and the Garou have other options besides Tribes to create spaces for specific minorities).</div> </div> </div> </div>So, your argument is, that the tribe is to large to have this right?<br /> The Black Furies are usually considered one of the smaller tribes of the Garou Nation, right?<br /> Their continued existence, as well as their revised depiction where they actively set to gain new members from other tribes, would indicate that certain demand for an all-girls club within the Garou Nation. Also, within the the game universe the tribe developed into being a tribe. Just like other groups, formerly camps, now are the majority of their respective tribes.<br /> <br /> What would be the limit of a tribe to be allowed to have some exclusivity regarding the gender of their members?<br /> 10, 100, 1000, 10.000 garou?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433380#post1433380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Black Furies can still have women's only spaces if they want them. They already have to do that with sub-groups within the Tribe because, again, the Tribe has men in it already. No &quot;rights&quot; have been robbed from them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the shift from exceptions to a rule to a change of the rule is a severe one.<br /> <br /> But what you are saying is, that a tribe of all female is not okay (not counting exceptions) but several camps are okay - based on what? I mean this distinction is completely arbitrary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433380#post1433380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this specific case, it can only exist if you also change the Tribe-as-written.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you say, but I can't see any evidence of that. The Black Furies, as written in revised and most likely W20 core, could very well<br /> 1. make exceptions for transgender people, just like they do for Metis<br /> 2. make exceptions for basically anyone they like,<br /> without abandoning their rule regarding membership completely. One would just have to state that exceptions are rare but possible. One doesn't have to change the tribe for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433380#post1433380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deplatforming them actually does wonders. But beyond that? Don't make them heroes in fiction seems like a no-brainer to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, what counts as &quot;make them heroes in fiction&quot;. Them simply being in the Tribebook? Or is it the way the troupe portraits them in their games?<br /> Is there actually fiction from the viewpoint of neo-Nazi Get anywhere? I mean in White Wolf or licensed products?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433380#post1433380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you were in charge of writing an RPG aimed at a German audience, and you don't like the rise of right-wing fascists, do you:<br /> A) Make sure to include more sympathetic representations of said political beliefs so people that have them feel reaffirmed that you believe their beliefs are good?<br /> or<br /> B) Make sure to depict such beliefs as dangerous and intolerable to a just society, hoping that some might see that it's a bad idea to go down that road, or at least you don't have to worry about about anyone else thinking you're encouraging them with your game?</div> </div> </div> </div>What about making an effort to show how dangerous political views are while also explaining how they came to be, meaning what social, political, historic and economic reasons allowed such dangerous views in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433380#post1433380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know people that avoid the game because they find the Kinfolk angle distasteful, yes. Lots of people know what it's like to live like a second class citizen even if the first class citizens mean well and don't generally treat you like shit. WtA doesn't really explore it well to make it compelling to use it to explore that for some people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it all comes down to how Kinfolk is depicted in the books, and sure, WtA didn't do a great job there. The problem is, that there are perfectly good depictions of garou/kinfolk relationships (my favourite of a scenario that makes sense is PGttG, and it is not written in universe), but also puts the spotlight on all the cases where it didn't work. Making victims of abuse the people of note in the Kinfolk: Unsung Heros book.<br /> Just like with the Get Neo-Nazis there is one element of the whole situation that is distracting from all the other aspects of the topic. Which is especially frustrating when these cases aren't meant to be the general state.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433380#post1433380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) One Gift not being able to tell the difference doesn't mean the game was changed to make it so nothing can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that was discussed a lot. And true, the Test Vial talen was copy&amp;pasted into W20 and the error, naming it a fetish wasn't even fixed. But, all the non-rules sections originally written for W20 sure deliver on the idea that it isn't possible (and never was).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433380#post1433380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing that KABA really did, and I don't see how it's a bad thing, was dedicate more space to what &quot;good&quot; kinfolk life is like, rather than what it isn't. It's a fairly important thing when setting the tone of prose. If you talk about the negatives, even if only as exceptions, they are what stick in people's minds. You need to talk about the positives as well so people treat the positives as the default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is a problem and should be solved. If KABA does a good job there, I'll take your word for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433380#post1433380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Black Furies aren't what those groups actually look like. Not now, not 60 years ago. Not 100 years ago. Not even longer. They're always coalition groups. Yes, the minority is in the center, and in the lead (at least if there's any chance of success historically speaking). Yes they want spaces where even the best allies don't need to be asked to not enter. But they always look for those allies. They bring those allies into the fold. That's part of reducing social stigma: companionship and kinship with people one step removed (and hopefully more as the movement grows). People they can trust and rely on. Those alliances aren't just social power, they're community, love, and friendship too.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But some Black Furies do that, too. I mean they have relationships with male kinfolk (even of other tribes) and form packs with males, even under Pegasus' patronage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T12:06:18-08:00","id":1433416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433361#post1433361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who's complaining about retconning out the neo-Nazi Get of Fenris?</div> </div> </div> </div>You set that strawman on fire! Went up in flames. Great job. Please clap.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T12:15:25-08:00","id":1433418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433393#post1433393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For as I wrote, Pegasus and the tribe should make exceptions for transgender people. They should imo not open their tribe to males in general, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>You also wrote: &quot;Instead of changing the tribe one should have created an option to address the matter and possibly give players a scenario to affect change within the tribe for there game if they wanted to, but still maintain the original state for those who don't want the change - or don't want the change dictated to them by a game designer.&quot;<br /> <br /> You're trying to have it both ways. You can't say that change is inherently wrong for the designers to do, and then say that an argument against the way the Tribe is doesn't count because you'd change it if you could.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, your argument is, that the tribe is to large to have this right? </div> </div> </div>No, I'm saying that a Tribe doesn't operate on the scale of an individual when discussing civics and just societies. Tribes are, in such a discussion, act on the scale of governments, not individuals. It doesn't matter if it's a small town of a hundred people, or a city of ten million people. A government that openly discriminates is not part of a just society.<br /> <br /> Do you feel that it is a rightful application of freedom of association, or a municipality to say that only people born without a penis may hold public office? Because that's what the Black Furies do. It's not about them having a woman's club for the local women to have a place to hang out with each other on their own terms, it's about how they define the governing structure of their culture.<br /> <br /> It really feels like you're not thinking this stuff out, and just posting whatever sounds good as a counterpoint in the moment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean this distinction is completely arbitrary. </div> </div> </div>See above, because the distinction is pretty painfully obvious to me: A Tribe is a government, a Camp is an association of like-minded individuals (which is normally internal to a Tribe, but doesn't have to be).<br /> <br /> How do you know this? Garou have to pick a Tribe or become, effectively, nationless people. You can try to pick a Tribe instead of going with the one you were born with (which isn't always going to work out how you hope, just like moving out of your home town isn't always going to work out either), but you have to pick a Tribe. Camps are optional groups no Garou is forced into (except for the rare cases they are and those Camps are then basically waiting to get killed off like the Cyberdogs).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One would just have to state that exceptions are rare but possible. One doesn't have to change the tribe for that. </div> </div> </div>The books say that exceptions beyond the existing Metis one are not possible. So you have to change the Tribe for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What about making an effort to show how dangerous political views are while also explaining how they came to be, meaning what social, political, historic and economic reasons allowed such dangerous views in the first place. </div> </div> </div>Dodging the question is noticeable.<br /> <br /> Also you're writing an RPG in this scenario, not a history book or essay on political movements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is especially frustrating when these cases aren't meant to be the general state. </div> </div> </div>Well... that's why new editions can be made to correct such issues....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, that was discussed a lot. And true, the Test Vial talen was copy&amp;pasted into W20 and the error, naming it a fetish wasn't even fixed. But, all the non-rules sections originally written for W20 sure deliver on the idea that it isn't possible (and never was). </div> </div> </div>You mean things like, &quot;The first application of the term is usually only used in retrospective, obviously, since it isn\u2019t typically possible to tell a pre-Change werewolf from a Kinfolk.&quot; Typically possible does not mean impossible. Though W20 suffers greatly from contradicting itself a lot on this matter. It still doesn't demonstrate your point on why this change was made. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> True. But some Black Furies do that, too. I mean they have relationships with male kinfolk (even of other tribes) and form packs with males, even under Pegasus' patronage. </div> </div> </div>Those aren't the same thing either.<br /> <br /> But the point is, that the Black Furies don't operate in a fashion that's actually coherent with their stated philosophy. Some of that can be pawned off on traditionalist sentiment from times where their operational methods were more appropriate for the times, but not all of it, and not indefinitely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T12:15:55-08:00","id":1433419,"title":"","content":"Plus, there are those who complain about that (expunging the Swords of Heimdall) \u2018sanitizing\u2019 the tribe\u2019s narrative as well. So, even from that angle, as ever, people will argue about anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T12:51:33-08:00","id":1433423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433416#post1433416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You set that strawman on fire! Went up in flames. Great job. Please clap.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm clapping happily as your stick your rhetorical foot in your mouth.<br /> <br /> It's not my fault you made a broad generalization that's easy to poke holes in. That doesn't make my counterpoint a strawman.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433419#post1433419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, there are those who complain about that (expunging the Swords of Heimdall) \u2018sanitizing\u2019 the tribe\u2019s narrative as well. So, even from that angle, as ever, people will argue about anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's W20 finally killing them off (though that's more of a metaplot thing than a strict retcon with how it's written), and then there's all the previous retcons of the Swords from initially being a mainstream Get camp, to deluded Get that took good ideas too far, to extremists shunned by any remotely rational Get. It was really hard to take the first attempts at retconing the Swords into &quot;bad Get&quot; for embracing genocide when the books were also saying that most Get feel the Wendigo and Uktena are cowards for &quot;fleeing&quot; west because they couldn't stand the strength of the Fenrir in light of the Fenrir's ancestors... participating in genociding the kinfolk of those Tribes; and also frequently being presented as hypocrites that fully embraced calling groups not traditionally part of their kin weaker races while saying that they don't care about things like skin color but about how well you can fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T13:56:20-08:00","id":1433426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433418#post1433418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You also wrote: &quot;Instead of changing the tribe one should have created an option to address the matter and possibly give players a scenario to affect change within the tribe for there game if they wanted to, but still maintain the original state for those who don't want the change - or don't want the change dictated to them by a game designer.&quot;<br /> <br /> You're trying to have it both ways. You can't say that change is inherently wrong for the designers to do, and then say that an argument against the way the Tribe is doesn't count because you'd change it if you could.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might think that, but my point would be, that even in earlier editions there were exceptions, the male metis. So extending this exception to the rule to transgender people would not be a change in tribal policy, since the issue wasn't even addressed before (at least not in my recollection). The tribe would largely remain as is, while still giving an official statement on the tribal policy, instead leaving it up to the individual STs.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, maybe that's having it both ways. Maybe it's compromise.<br /> <br /> Was there even a need to have this officially mandated in a book? I mean, if an ST wants to have an transgender NPC or a Player wants to play a transgeder Black Fury, shouldn't they make the decision? I kinda feel that making an official statement in a book for something that isn't going to happen very often is - at the risk of offending one party or the other, is kind of a bad move.<br /> Because, with an official statement, one is trying to force one's own political views towards the players, as opposed to leaving these issues for them to decide as they like it.<br /> <br /> That's why I am pro &quot;sidebar with options&quot; in regard to this topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433418#post1433418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm saying that a Tribe doesn't operate on the scale of an individual when discussing civics and just societies. Tribes are, in such a discussion, act on the scale of governments, not individuals. It doesn't matter if it's a small town of a hundred people, or a city of ten million people. A government that openly discriminates is not part of a just society.<br /> <br /> Do you feel that it is a rightful application of freedom of association, or a municipality to say that only people born without a penis may hold public office? Because that's what the Black Furies do. It's not about them having a woman's club for the local women to have a place to hang out with each other on their own terms, it's about how they define the governing structure of their culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here we come back to the problem with not discerning pre-change garou anymore.<br /> <br /> Up to revised edition, only male kinfolk would remain with the Black Fury community, while male garou would be given away as babies and therefore there wouldn't be the problem that male garou would be without the right to fully be members of their society.<br /> <br /> Now, in W20, males would be part of Black Fury communities up until they have a first change and be then unable to join the tribe. I can see, how in this case the tribe is actually denying parts of their group rights, which would be unjust. A scenario that wouldn't happen otherwise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433418#post1433418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really feels like you're not thinking this stuff out, and just posting whatever sounds good as a counterpoint in the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just think you have some very different ideas of some aspects of the game, than I have.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433418#post1433418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See above, because the distinction is pretty painfully obvious to me: A Tribe is a government, a Camp is an association of like-minded individuals (which is normally internal to a Tribe, but doesn't have to be).<br /> <br /> How do you know this? Garou have to pick a Tribe or become, effectively, nationless people. You can try to pick a Tribe instead of going with the one you were born with (which isn't always going to work out how you hope, just like moving out of your home town isn't always going to work out either), but you have to pick a Tribe. Camps are optional groups no Garou is forced into (except for the rare cases they are and those Camps are then basically waiting to get killed off like the Cyberdogs).</div> </div> </div> </div>We went over the fact, that sometimes the tribe is chosen for you. In my mind it was totally clear up to this point that there would never be male garou cubs to be raised within Black Fury communities, period. The tribe books tell us, these children are given away to other tribes. Therefore these kids would be raised with this other tribe and belong to it and never have any loss, regarding their inability to join the Black Furies.<br /> <br /> But, with W20, this becomes kind of different, I guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433418#post1433418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The books say that exceptions beyond the existing Metis one are not possible. So you have to change the Tribe for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still not as fundamental a change as allowing the admittance of males in general. Also, I feel that a &quot;You asked about trnasgenders? Well, we never taught about it before, but we guess you could handle them as exceptions like male metis, if you feel this is appropriate.&quot; is a much more honest passage in a Black Fury write-up than changing the tribe's philosophy entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433418#post1433418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dodging the question is noticeable.</div> </div> </div> </div>As noticeable as giving two black and white answers to answer a highly complex topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433418#post1433418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also you're writing an RPG in this scenario, not a history book or essay on political movements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, WtA tribes and camps are tied to stereotypes of real world ethnic and political groups and movements. So, I feel it should be nuanced representation of the matter, even in a RPG scenario.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433418#post1433418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... that's why new editions can be made to correct such issues....</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, the matter of discussion is how to correct them. What is the new normal, and what level of decisions are left to STs and their troupes and what is a change brought into the game forcefully.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433418#post1433418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean things like, &quot;The first application of the term is usually only used in retrospective, obviously, since it isn\u2019t typically possible to tell a pre-Change werewolf from a Kinfolk.&quot; Typically possible does not mean impossible. Though W20 suffers greatly from contradicting itself a lot on this matter. It still doesn't demonstrate your point on why this change was made.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it goes right on with: &quot;Rumor has it that certain divinatory rites once allowed certain knowledge of whether a child would eventually Change, but if these rites ever existed, they are lost to modern Garou. The best the People can do is keep tabs on their children and wait.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, this really reads like<br /> 1.) We retcon that pre-change cubs are discernable from kinfolk<br /> 2.) All mentions of abilities to do so in W20 are there, because we Copy&amp;Pasted stuff.<br /> <br /> Do you, personally, if you ST a W20 WtA game allow players to have their characters' parents raise them as garou, because they knew, or not?<br /> And would you allow PCs a means to determine their characters kinds species, if they have kids?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T15:36:53-08:00","id":1433428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433426#post1433426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, yeah, maybe that's having it both ways. Maybe it's compromise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regardless, you're changing the Tribe even if you don't feel like it's a significant change, and the logic behind doing so doesn't hold up to the counterarguments against other changes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Was there even a need to have this officially mandated in a book? </div> </div> </div>You do remember is thread is about W20 Changing Ways, and one of the shitty things about that book is the WW inserts about trans werewolves? And that some Black Furies kill trans women Garou because TERFy bullshit? That it's a mainstream belief in the Garou Nation that being trans is an affront to Gaia?<br /> <br /> In the same book that points out (in the parts that aren't a WW insert) Garou can be shaped into whatever sexual form they want if they ask the right spirits nicely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, if an ST wants to have an transgender NPC or a Player wants to play a transgeder Black Fury, shouldn't they make the decision? </div> </div> </div>They shouldn't have to feel like they're house-ruling the game to do so though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I kinda feel that making an official statement in a book for something that isn't going to happen very often is - at the risk of offending one party or the other, is kind of a bad move. </div> </div> </div>I see nothing wrong with offending anyone that would get offended by the idea that the Black Furies are fully accepting of trans women as women. Basic Intolerance Paradox stuff here. If a game caters to transphobic views, than they're ceding the fandom to transphobes.<br /> <br /> What you're talking about it how we get messy things like W20 Changing Ways, or some of the really cringing V5 passages: writers trying to both sides things in a game that isn't shy about being political in its message doesn't work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because, with an official statement, one is trying to force one's own political views towards the players, as opposed to leaving these issues for them to decide as they like it. </div> </div> </div>The WoD has always had a very strong political bias and has never been shy about that. The books are full of official statements that carry strong political views and ones that they're not saying should just be left to the table to decide about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Up to revised edition, only male kinfolk would remain with the Black Fury community, while male garou would be given away as babies and therefore there wouldn't be the problem that male garou would be without the right to fully be members of their society. </div> </div> </div>That's shifting the goal-post significantly. And regardless of edition male born Garou of Black Furies can still easily find out they were born to a Black Fury or Black Fury bloodline, and have to deal with that load of baggage. The Rite of Heritage is a thing, and Pure Breed is a thing.<br /> <br /> Are you going to answer the question?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We went over the fact, that sometimes the tribe is chosen for you. </div> </div> </div>Which... doesn't address what I said. Tribes are governments (I didn't get to pick what country I'm a citizen of by birth, and my options of immigration are limited), Camps are social associations, when talking about civics and just societies. Are you actually disagreeing with this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still not as fundamental a change as allowing the admittance of males in general. </div> </div> </div>Well, that highly depends on a personal perspective, but yes, I'd agree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As noticeable as giving two black and white answers to answer a highly complex topic. </div> </div> </div>Some answers are simple even if the problem is complex. Sometimes, in rhetoric, you seek to simplify things because it's clear that you're going to have people try to drown out the actual points at hand with appeals to nuance or complexity; if we can't discuss the simplified version, there's not much that's going to happen with trying to discuss things with the totality of nuance on the table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, I feel it should be nuanced representation of the matter, even in a RPG scenario. </div> </div> </div>And yet you're arguing on the side of not making the Black Furies a more nuanced representation of the real world issues they reflect. So how does that work?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you, personally, if you ST a W20 WtA game allow players to have their characters' parents raise them as garou, because they knew, or not?<br /> And would you allow PCs a means to determine their characters kinds species, if they have kids? </div> </div> </div>I, personally, house rule out a lot of it. I keep the ritual aspect of being able to do so, but not the &quot;instant recognition via a Rank 1 Gift,&quot; part. It's the best of both worlds as all the material/backwards compatibility that keys of the Garou being able to do so if valid, but making it harder to do has some narrative benefits towards things like Lost Cubs and missing a pre-changer among kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-25T18:12:47-08:00","id":1433441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433428#post1433428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do remember is thread is about W20 Changing Ways, and one of the shitty things about that book is the WW inserts about trans werewolves? And that some Black Furies kill trans women Garou because TERFy bullshit? That it's a mainstream belief in the Garou Nation that being trans is an affront to Gaia?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I can see some Black Furies kill transgender, or trans women as a possibility within the game world - although I wouldn't necessarily limit such misguided behaviour to Black Furies I can see why they were singled out.<br /> <br /> I find the statement that garou would see being trans as an affront to Gaia as severely misguided.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433428#post1433428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They shouldn't have to feel like they're house-ruling the game to do so though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I suggest a wording that indicates each option is completely valid and only up to what the ST and troupe find suitable for their game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433428#post1433428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see nothing wrong with offending anyone that would get offended by the idea that the Black Furies are fully accepting of trans women as women. Basic Intolerance Paradox stuff here. If a game caters to transphobic views, than they're ceding the fandom to transphobes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant in regards to full membership for any male person. As I said, the Black Furies should accept trans women. As a tribe that values personal freedom and choices, any TERF behaviour should be only seen in a small minority, if at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433428#post1433428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's shifting the goal-post significantly. And regardless of edition male born Garou of Black Furies can still easily find out they were born to a Black Fury or Black Fury bloodline, and have to deal with that load of baggage. The Rite of Heritage is a thing, and Pure Breed is a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Rite of Heritage was only in the Get of Fenris TB pre-W20.<br /> <br /> Also, Pure Breed is tribal specific and spiritual, not biological. As Ehtan once pointed out in the old White Wolf forums. That is why TB Black Furies author, imo, screwed up, when he wrote about pure breed Silver Fangs with black fur (indicating males born to Black Furies).<br /> <br /> Sure, if a player wants to have a male who was given up by the furies, raised by another tribe and then still explore his heritage, then this is a topic to develop a side plot around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433428#post1433428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you going to answer the question?</div> </div> </div> </div>The question if penises should be grounds to be barred from public office. Thought that was rhetoric. Obviously, this shouldn't happen, if males are part of society and thereby barred from all public office. Within the garou nation, this wouldn't be the case, though, if only the Black Furies barred their membership. <br /> <br /> Strangely enough, I never heard that any company or public agency in Germany had a male officer for equality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433428#post1433428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which... doesn't address what I said. Tribes are governments (I didn't get to pick what country I'm a citizen of by birth, and my options of immigration are limited), Camps are social associations, when talking about civics and just societies. Are you actually disagreeing with this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know with the rev TB there were the two governing bodies for the whole tribe introduced. Still, I don't see tribes as I see governments. For me, septs are the governing entity of the garou's everyday's life. I can't really describe the status the tribe has, in my opinion, on the life of a garou. Certainly not that the tribe is a entity that changes policy formally or something like that.<br /> <br /> [QUOTE=Heavy Arms;n1433428]Some answers are simple even if the problem is complex. Sometimes, in rhetoric, you seek to simplify things because it's clear that you're going to have people try to drown out the actual points at hand with appeals to nuance or complexity; if we can't discuss the simplified version, there's not much that's going to happen with trying to discuss things with the totality of nuance on the table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433428#post1433428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet you're arguing on the side of not making the Black Furies a more nuanced representation of the real world issues they reflect. So how does that work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Am I?<br /> I argue that a strict female yes/male no approach to tribal membership is probably leaving people with questions. So, there should be an explanation and examples given, how incorporation of transgender people is handled by the tribe. Doesn't mean that I think the tribe should change to incorporate any male...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T17:38:45-08:00","id":1433753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433423#post1433423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm clapping happily as your stick your rhetorical foot in your mouth.<br /> <br /> It's not my fault you made a broad generalization that's easy to poke holes in. That doesn't make my counterpoint a strawman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your comment doesn't do that at all. You just did what you always do when you get into a prolonged debate with people who don't agree with you. You resort to gross exaggeration, selective evidence, slipshod logic, and moving goal posts as you completely avoid other people's arguments and repeat your own premises again and again. Then you become increasingly upset and abusive to the other board members because they don't hold your opinions. I've lost count how often you succumb to this. People just can't hold different opinions or interpretations than you after a certain point - they're objectively wrong, perhaps even morally wrong, and you insist they bow down to your superior wisdom. That your tactics never seem to succeed in changing anyone's opinion doesn't affect you in the slightest. You just declare victory and do a victory lap as everyone looks on perplexed. It's a shame as in other threads you genuinely engage in real dialogue and help people with your knowledge of the game. But only you know why you act the way you do.<br /> <br /> Of course your argument is a strawman, and it's one on multiple levels.<br /> <br /> First, we're talking about a totem and how it impacts tribal membership. You insert something about Nazis even though there is nothing at the totem level about Nazis. This was clearly an issue of homids coming in from certain human cultures after a certain historical time period. If the Get has a simple identity that people classify the tribe as, it's not &quot;Neo-Nazi werewolves&quot;, it's &quot;Viking werewolves.&quot;<br /> <br /> Second, even your generalization of the Get of Fenris as Neo-Nazis is wrong. You said the Get of Fenris depicted Neo-Nazis as one of the good guys. This is objectively wrong. The game did mention that the Get of Fenris had white supremacists as members, but always mentioned this was a bad thing. First edition corebook said it brought &quot;undying shame&quot; to the tribe. And in the same paragraphed that mentioned, it also stated that the Get was including more racial minorities that fit them. How does that depict them as good guys or even as a defining element? Even within the context of Garou culture - not the human culture of the players - this was seen as a problem. When the first edition Players Guide came out and revealed the Sword of Heimdall camp, again it presented them as bad and even said it was not meant for PCs, meaning these were NPC antagonists. And an early depiction of such an NPC - Aeschylus/Pink Tom - Rage Across Across New York, is clearly not any kind of good guy. He's clearly a villain and antagonist in the setting, filled with hate for others because of the self-hatred and feelings of abandonment he feels towards himself. Every tribe in the early days of the game had a camp that was explicitly &quot;Wyrmish&quot;. Obvious antagonists within the tribe who usually represented the worst of that tribe. The Swords were simply that camp for the Get. So your claims that Neo-Nazis were presented as bad guys, or that it was somehow representative of the tribe as a whole is just false. I've never heard anyone say that they couldn't play the game or couldn't play the Get because simply because a group of villains were included as part of the setting.<br /> <br /> Third, the elimination of the Swords of Heimdall occurred at the same time the game downplayed ALL of those Wyrm camps in the Revised era. The Man Eaters were also wiped out. The Eaters of the Dead and Bitter Hex were downgraded to secret societies. The Fianna's camps were reinterpreted to move beyond human politics. The Bringers of Eternal Peace were now said to be outright Black Spiral Dancers. Instead of these camps being a display as a problem within the tribe, they were either changed/revised/expanded or made outright enemies. No one says that the Man Eaters were removed because players didn't want to play cannibals. Now I did hear that some LARPs were having troubles because local skinheads would show up to play Sword of Heimdall Get as an excuse to publicly propagate their Nazism and hide between &quot;I'm just roleplaying my character.&quot; So there could be other motives in Revised's metaplot, or it might just be pretext. There are always going to be shitbags like that causing trouble and hiding behind &quot;it's only roleplay.&quot; And the answer to that is always the same - remove disruptive people from the game. It's an OOC issue, not an IC issue.<br /> <br /> And none of these changes, of course, were retcons. They did not retroactively change the past of the tribe that was previously established. They were metaplot changes. They introduce changes in the game, but changes that came out of new character actions and events - not suddenly rewriting the past or changing the nature of the totem to something different than what it had been. What was being retconned out? That Neo-Nazis never existed? That World War II never happened? In W20, the Swords of Heimdall are still mentioned in the corebook as a camp, with the usual caveats that portray them as villains. So even a weak version of your argument doesn't even hold true.<br /> <br /> I think many STs ignore some or even all elements of the metaplot from Revised. What elements they want to retain, change, or include is just part of the typical job of the ST. But that's a different discussion than the role of the totem in defining requirements to be a member of the tribe.<br /> <br /> But enjoy your victory lap. I've already left the stadium along with everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-28T19:01:10-08:00","id":1433757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1433753#post1433753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But only you know why you act the way you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because people like you have a very negative effect on my caring about my phrasing because I'll be roundly ad hominem lambasted no matter what I say, what you said, or any of that, because I've been declared an &quot;Internet Asshole,&quot; and everything I post is always read as uncharitably as possible so when people don't like the conclusions they get to blame me for nastiness of their own invention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First, we're talking about a totem and how it impacts tribal membership. </div> </div> </div>Nope. The neo-Nazi thing was about retcons, not Totems and membership. A response to the specific claim about how people react to retcons is not a strawman just because it doesn't apply to the issues of Tribal membership that the retcon thing was a tangent of.<br /> <br /> A strawman is if I'm arguing against something you didn't say, but making it look like I am, so I can defeat the similar-but-improper argument instead of the one you made.<br /> <br /> Even if you disagree with my example:<br /> <br /> &quot;People don't like retcons.&quot;<br /> &quot;This is a retcon people liked.&quot;<br /> <br /> Is not a strawman, regardless of the larger context of the discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, even your generalization of the Get of Fenris as Neo-Nazis is wrong. </div> </div> </div>See, this is a strawman, though at least I could see it as a honest mistake in other circumstances. &quot;The neo-Nazi Get of Fenris,&quot; could be read as, &quot;The Get of Fenris, who are neo-Nazis,&quot; or, &quot;the neo-Nazis who are also Get of Fenris.&quot; My argument was not, &quot;the whole Tribe was neo-Nazis, and then retconed into that not being so,&quot; but that the game consistently retconned the support for neo-Nazism within the Tribe to be lesser than it was originally written (and as I noted before, even the 1e books trying to say that the Swords were horrible need to be put into context of them being denounced by in-character people that still believe in racist ideologies). I could be more charitable about this, but my response to Gryphon15 was clearly not included in your analysis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've already left the stadium along with everyone else. </div> </div> </div>If you've left the stadium as it were... why even bother posting this?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-31T14:26:05-08:00","id":1434044,"title":"","content":"I think the problem with the neo-Nazi-ties Gets might have, as well as behaviour of garou towards kinfolk and a lot of other topics do stem, to no small piece, from the in-universe viewpoint of some of the source material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-12T11:34:19-08:00","id":1435306,"title":"","content":"Not sure why I've been un-banned prior to the stated time, but I have been given time to cool off and think this through. there are two great problems with BF accepting trans women: <br /> <br /> 1- If Pegasus accepts trans women, how do these initiates cope with a society that would assume they are Metis? Think about it for a moment, you see a Black Fury that looks biologically male. Metis are 1/10th the garou population. Trans individuals make up 0.5% of the population (optimistic estimates give about a 1%) and thus, ignoring other factors, Male metis outnumber trans-women by a factor of 10 or 20. Imagine having to explain to every Garou you meet that you're not a metis and shouldn't be treated like crap for it. You're basically signing up for double discrimination. <br /> <br /> 2- If Pegasus works along the lines of gender rather than sex, and thus includes trans-women, would pegasus not be obligated to deny trans-men from joining the tribe? You can't have your cake and eat it too, or at least, if you do want to allow both trans-men and trans-women into the black furies, then it just sounds like pegasus is pulling all the bullshit excuses it can to specifically exclude and attack cis men, and that hardly feels like a constructive attitude to sex and gender. Sounds Wyrmy, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-12T13:04:22-08:00","id":1435309,"title":"","content":"Are Black Furies accepting any trans person, or only Male-to-female transgender people?<br /> I would assume the latter, if we are talking about a version of the tribe that is not open to males in general.<br /> I'd also guess that they accept all members that are biologically female, even if they identify as non-binary or something else.<br /> I'd further assume that a garou who after being part of the Black Furies dermines that she is in her heart and soul male and wants to life as such (wether ot not this includes a biological alteration to the body through science or a spirit, or a wizard, or something) would leave the tribe. Because, it would be the honourable thing to do.<br /> <br /> But if a garou who was female, and a Black Fury, would discovers/decides that she is really a he, than he would have to live with the fact that he might be mistaken for a Metis. Then again with a tribe of maybe 2000 garou worldwide, one percent would be 20 garou in total. I would guess people would know pretty fast who was the transgender in their tribe in their part of the world....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-12T13:35:26-08:00","id":1435311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1435306#post1435306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Pegasus accepts trans women, how do these initiates cope with a society that would assume they are Metis?</div> </div> </div> </div>According to Changing Ways 20 trans Garou already face this (and worse) regardless of Tribe. Pegasus accepting them would decrease the current default prejudice against them in the game (and mean that no Black Fury that wants to stay a Black Fury could tolerate trans Garou being murdered by other Garou for being trans). <br /> <br /> Of course, remember that they are, officially, spirits that can give Garou magic sexual reassignment that are vastly superior to what human medical science can do. The Black Furies, Children of Gaia, and whoever else feels like getting in can just get some Theurges together, develop a specialized version of the Summoning rite, and let trans Garou have the bodies they want to have and after it's over they wouldn't have to worry about being seen as &quot;Metis&quot; by anyone. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're basically signing up for double discrimination. </div> </div> </div>No. You're facing extra discrimination regardless, because you're not &quot;signing up&quot; to be trans. Changing Pegasus and the Black Furies to be more accepting of trans Garou is adding spaces of less discrimination to the Nation, not taking them away.<br /> <br /> Trans people already live in a world that gives them shit, and the current state of the Garou Nation in the books is even worse than humanity about it (sounds Wyrmy to me?). Making even part of the Nation less shitty to trans Garou is not making discrimination worse; claiming otherwise is being absolutely blind to the discrimination that's already there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2- If Pegasus works along the lines of gender rather than sex, and thus includes trans-women, would pegasus not be obligated to deny trans-men from joining the tribe? </div> </div> </div>Pegasus can accept cis-male Metis into the Tribe just fine. Pegasus can make whatever exceptions or standards the writers of the material want them to make.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...then it just sounds like pegasus is pulling all the bullshit excuses it can to specifically exclude and attack cis men, and that hardly feels like a constructive attitude to sex and gender. </div> </div> </div>And? I've already pointed out that the logical extension of treating the Black Furies as a Tribe with thousands of years of history, and Pegasus as a spirit with a consistent thematic nature would mean that the &quot;All female-but-not-really&quot; Black Furies of the 1e book doesn't make sense as how the Tribe operates. Hence all my issues with WtA's Tribes all being cool stereotypes that had patchwork back-filling in to try to turn them into fully fleshed out social entities leading to all sorts of problematic content (from lots of different takes on what problematic can mean).<br /> <br /> If WtA was world-built first, I'm very much of the opinion that the Black Furies, if even kept as a Tribe, would have had the sex/gender exclusivity part dropped during development, and the Tribe would have been dropped for a conservatively matriarchal society instead (with internal struggles such as maintaining matriarchal traditions vs. being true to their mission as defenders of the oppressed and not oppressing their own male members as well as fighting to help men damaged by toxic patriarchy in the world rather than just kicking ass for women).<br /> <br /> And of course, a rebooted retelling of the Black Furies can actually incorporate groups like the Scythians, who might have been the actual inspiration of the Amazons, and had mixed gender armies that apparently certain ancient Greeks couldn't wrap their heads around and had to invent the idea of an all woman tribe to justify having women soldiers (and then made sure the Amazons always get beaten by male Greek heroes because sexism). Pulling more from the western horse-people of Eurasia like the Scythians also gives them a stronger connection to Pegasus, and opens up some more interesting Gift options for making the Black Furies unique of they come from a tradition of horseback archers as their primary mode of military fighting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-13T05:45:46-08:00","id":1435351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1435311#post1435311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> And? I've already pointed out that the logical extension of treating the Black Furies as a Tribe with thousands of years of history, and Pegasus as a spirit with a consistent thematic nature would mean that the &quot;All female-but-not-really&quot; Black Furies of the 1e book doesn't make sense as how the Tribe operates. Hence all my issues with WtA's Tribes all being cool stereotypes that had patchwork back-filling in to try to turn them into fully fleshed out social entities leading to all sorts of problematic content (from lots of different takes on what problematic can mean).<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>We can certainly agree on this at least. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If WtA was world-built first, I'm very much of the opinion that the Black Furies, if even kept as a Tribe, would have had the sex/gender exclusivity part dropped during development </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure on this, and I don't mind the concept of a men-exclusionary tribe (even if it is a very serious problem in terms of getting the numbers up; it's difficult to imagine them ever avoiding the backfoot in an inter-tribal war*, even though they're one of the most doped-up tribes when it comes to combat gifts and gnarly fetishes) <br /> *from other tribes only increases wars fought<br /> <br /> I think an important caveat though is some sort of... story is needed to justify the no (cis?) men rule. Yeah they don't want men and don't like men. That's not enough. I want a good justification why I can't make a Homid male black fury. Is it Pegasus being petty over losing his balls? Is it Pegasus going far-too-in on embracing femininity? Is pegasus overcompensating and wishes to see himself as a chinese emperor surrounded by a thousand women and a few trusted eunuchs? is the man-exclusion a trade-off from some grand covenant with certain spirits for exceptional power, Were the tribe founders bitter man-haters that threw it into their tribe constitution, and perhaps enforced the rule with a spirit covenant? Motive is just as important as action, and we lack a clear motive, so it's really difficult to accept the decision or work on a how-to-fix when we don't really know the reason behind the bullshit. I mean, you seem to be working from the perspective that Pegasus is a good woman, while I seem to have come under the cynical persuasion that pegasus'd be just another spirit with his own, perhaps irrational, self interests in mind. An in-universe explanation would be a necessary lampshade to avoid the feeling that the writers are just pouring in their own personal values and screwing people that don't align with them. </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-13T08:11:33-08:00","id":1435360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1435351#post1435351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not so sure on this, and I don't mind the concept of a men-exclusionary tribe...</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is, of course, the word &quot;tribe.&quot; The idea of all sorts of exclusionary packs, camps, and so on? Sure, works fine. But a tribe (or a Tribe) doesn't really make sense as giving up on half of their born potential members, in the hopes that they'll replace those numbers with women Garou of other Tribes (only on other Tribe is noted as having any particular problem with keeping their women Garou, and even then the Valkyries have never actually fully rejected the Get).<br /> <br /> That's why I said it would get dumped in development. The idea is evocative and cool, but it doesn't hold up when you try to actually world build them into existence. Growing from a single pack of all women Garou in pre-history Greece following the spirits of the Greek mythological Furies, to a full Tribe can't really happen with the men-exclusion part. Where are all these women Garou coming from? Why do they want to join up with the proto-BFs who were focused on getting revenge for wronged women specifically instead of all the cultural values they were raised with by their birth Tribes?<br /> <br /> I brought up the Scythians because there's this image of women having no power in ancient Eurasia, because of the very patriarchal empires that wrote a lot of the history, and wrote out a lot of cultures that were clearly not as gender segregated (many of which were enemies of the Greeks and Persians). Why wouldn't the Furies be influenced by those societies where women weren't regulated to property of men, seeing how a more egalitarian society was possible (even if history saw them get conquered in the end)? One of the things I've repeatedly tried to stress is that the ancient world the Black Furies began in, wasn't the Athenian propaganda that was perpetuated by Hellenistic historians.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think an important caveat though is some sort of... story is needed to justify the no (cis?) men rule. </div> </div> </div>And one that doesn't fall apart with things like the Metis exception.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-13T12:07:56-08:00","id":1435377,"title":"","content":"I disagree. It is often said, that a tribe that sends away half his potential members would have problems and so on. But, there is one simple fact about the Tribe. The Tribe is not only garou, it's kinfolk, too. And male kinfolk is present in the Tribe. So, with a quote of about one true bread child in 10 kids, they give away not half of their children but 5% of them. This, of course, means that the Black Furies have an unnatural low ratio of garou to kinfolk, but are still a sustainable community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-14T01:33:14-08:00","id":1435429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1435360#post1435360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And one that doesn't fall apart with things like the Metis exception.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Pegasus doesn't like people with working sperm production&quot; works with the metis exception. (and 'Pegasus doesn't want people to geld themselves' keeps the homids/lupus who want to change out) Infact, this is the only story I can think up that really matches up and fits the criteria we need: It fits Pegasus's story, and it explains why metis are an exception. You can surely justify some non-bio essentialist rational, but it wouldn't be so simple, and simple explanations are best.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1435377#post1435377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. It is often said, that a tribe that sends away half his potential members would have problems and so on. But, there is one simple fact about the Tribe. The Tribe is not only garou, it's kinfolk, too. And male kinfolk is present in the Tribe. So, with a quote of about one true bread child in 10 kids, they give away not half of their children but 5% of them. This, of course, means that the Black Furies have an unnatural low ratio of garou to kinfolk, but are still a sustainable community.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe Garou stay honourably mated, and the rule is probably flouted in at least in the much-larger tribes like the Fianna, the CoG, and the Gnawers. Garou are half human, exceptionally attractive, and power drunk. If we look at just numbers, then the Garou (1/10th chance of breeding true) and the kinfolk (1/100 chance of breeding true, but there are ten times more kinfolk) are equal providers of new garou. But that doesn't take into account that male garou are probably getting more than a fair share. Even if you're under the impression that they are, you have to compound things. Let's say the prehistoric Get of Fenrir is in a breeding race with BF because they wanna have more numbers for a war against them. For simplicity sake, we're talking homid/human couples, and we'll assume they're ten-times more likely to breed true so i can keep numbers small, and we're not going to discuss any extranious variables like willingness to breed or whatnot; The Get start with a male and female garou, and about a hundred kinfolk, whilst the BF start with a female garou and a hundred kinfolk . After the first 'round' the get now have three garou and 20 kinfolk, the BF have 2 garou and 20 kinfolk. After the second round the Get have 8 garou and 40 kinfolk, the black Furies have four garou and 40 kinfolk. After the third round the get have 20 garou and 80 kinfolk, while the black furies have eight garou and eighty kinfolk. at the 4th round... the Get have 48 garou, and the black furies have 16 garou. The Get have three times as many garou. This only gets worse as you go up, and it gets worse when you add 'realism' variables like how willing each party is to have kids, lupus... if these two tribes had a skirmish the BF would most probably lose, other tribes may get involved.... Unless the BF have some seriously powerful -what-were-the-apis-even-for- super fertility rites that they traded their men for, it's really miraculous that as one of the most fighty tribes the BF survived till the modern day without being wiped by their rivals. After all the Fianna, of all tribes, lost most of it's territory on continental europe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-14T07:52:42-08:00","id":1435451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1435429#post1435429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Pegasus doesn't like people with working sperm production&quot; works with the metis exception.</div> </div> </div> </div>But not with expanding the Tribe to include trans Garou; esp. if you want to avoid the ugly minefield that is judging someones gender by their status vis a vis sex reassignment.<br /> <br /> Can a cis-male Homid that suffered the gelded battle-scar join the Black Furies? Or just one born impotent because even for the Garou somethings that sort of thing happens?<br /> <br /> It isn't really a story if it's just a torture paragraph of justifications for how &quot;Some asshole cut my balls off, so I'm going to exclude people from my Tribe based on this very precise criteria,&quot; should be accepted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can surely justify some non-bio essentialist rational, but it wouldn't be so simple, and simple explanations are best. </div> </div> </div>Complete explanations are the best; simple but not actually explaining isn't better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This only gets worse as you go up, and it gets worse when you add 'realism' variables like how willing each party is to have kids, lupus... if these two tribes had a skirmish the BF would most probably lose, other tribes may get involved.... Unless the BF have some seriously powerful -what-were-the-apis-even-for- super fertility rites that they traded their men for, it's really miraculous that as one of the most fighty tribes the BF survived till the modern day without being wiped by their rivals. After all the Fianna, of all tribes, lost most of it's territory on continental europe. </div> </div> </div>Yes, this exactly.<br /> <br /> It's not that the BFs can't have a society in a vacuum if they get rid of their men Garou, it's that in the context of the game, where the early Tribes were constantly in competition (frequently violent and deadly competition) they can't afford to toss away half of their Garou for some paltry trickle of women Garou from other Tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-14T09:47:20-08:00","id":1435462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1435451#post1435451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But not with expanding the Tribe to include trans Garou; esp. if you want to avoid the ugly minefield that is judging someones gender by their status vis a vis sex reassignment.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me at least, doesn't matter if WW decide to include or exclude trans-men, we need something that utterly internalizes this decision as an eternal aspect of the setting, and not something that's obviously a writer telling us all to interpret something this way. <br /> <br /> -&quot;Pegasus is a stuborn prick, we'd like to do something about it, but we can't&quot; (obviosly nobody'd talk about their totem that way but you can keep the sentiment) <br /> -&quot;We have a magic means to transition, if you're not a metis you must go through it before joining, actually we try to poach trans-women from other tribes with this method. We used to keep this a secret&quot;. <br /> -&quot;Trans exclusion was really something put into place by the old-guard, it wasn't on Pegasus. Now that they're being phased out, and we're desperate for members...&quot; <br /> <br /> I just fear we'll get something too... lazy. &quot;pegasus called, (s)he said trans-women are in, anyone who disagrees or causes strife will become a Bone Gnawer...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-14T12:12:14-08:00","id":1435476,"title":"","content":"I have very little care about how W5 phrases things. I'll read it, like I read V5, but it's going to have to make me want to consider trying to marry a book if it wants to earn me as a customer.<br /> <br /> I care more about what I can do in my games to fix things from the existing editions that never got fixed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-14T14:39:09-08:00","id":1435483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1435429#post1435429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe Garou stay honourably mated, and the rule is probably flouted in at least in the much-larger tribes like the Fianna, the CoG, and the Gnawers. Garou are half human, exceptionally attractive, and power drunk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, no and no.<br /> There is nothing in the Setting stating they are exceptionally attractive. There is a obscure rule that they can use Rage to make someone have sex with them, and we discussed in other topics if this is date rape or not. There is also no indication, that garou strive for more and more power or are by any means, in general, becoming drunk on power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1435429#post1435429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we look at just numbers, then the Garou (1/10th chance of breeding true) and the kinfolk (1/100 chance of breeding true, but there are ten times more kinfolk) are equal providers of new garou. But that doesn't take into account that male garou are probably getting more than a fair share. Even if you're under the impression that they are, you have to compound things. Let's say the prehistoric Get of Fenrir is in a breeding race with BF because they wanna have more numbers for a war against them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Get or any garou aren't Walder Frey, who can have his sons fight your sons and if all of them are dead he still has twenty-three sons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1435429#post1435429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For simplicity sake, we're talking homid/human couples, and we'll assume they're ten-times more likely to breed true so i can keep numbers small, and we're not going to discuss any extranious variables like willingness to breed or whatnot; The Get start with a male and female garou, and about a hundred kinfolk, whilst the BF start with a female garou and a hundred kinfolk . After the first 'round' the get now have three garou and 20 kinfolk, the BF have 2 garou and 20 kinfolk. After the second round the Get have 8 garou and 40 kinfolk, the black Furies have four garou and 40 kinfolk. After the third round the get have 20 garou and 80 kinfolk, while the black furies have eight garou and eighty kinfolk. at the 4th round... the Get have 48 garou, and the black furies have 16 garou. The Get have three times as many garou. This only gets worse as you go up, and it gets worse when you add 'realism' variables like how willing each party is to have kids, lupus... if these two tribes had a skirmish the BF would most probably lose, other tribes may get involved.... Unless the BF have some seriously powerful -what-were-the-apis-even-for- super fertility rites that they traded their men for, it's really miraculous that as one of the most fighty tribes the BF survived till the modern day without being wiped by their rivals. After all the Fianna, of all tribes, lost most of it's territory on continental europe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or that any tribe survived givent he numbers the BSD might have...<br /> <br /> But, you whole math example is flawed. It doesn't take into account that Get tend to have deadly Rites of Passages. Black Furies willingness to adopt females into the tribe, while Get of Fenris might not care for your skin colour, as long as one of your ancestors, preferably a parent, was Get. Also, the Get of Fenris might not make use of fertility charms in a way, the Black Furies might.<br /> <br /> That said, I totally acknowledge that the Black Furies are one of the smaller Tribes within the Setting. But I oppose the argument that they need to open to male members of any kind (as opposed to Metis and some other rare exceptions) to survive. That is, unless one fundamentally changes the chance of a child breeding true significantly from what is given in 2nd and revised.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-14T15:53:47-08:00","id":1435490,"title":"","content":"You're talking now. We're talking in the distant past before things got how they got now. When things like the Tribes actively warring with each other for control over Caerns and kinfolk communities was a thing. When the Tribes weren't widely distributed and very few Septs had more than one Tribe in them; so the idea that women could just go join the Black Furies wasn't really an option for most Garou to consider.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-15T00:59:58-08:00","id":1435523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1435490#post1435490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're talking now. We're talking in the distant past before things got how they got now. When things like the Tribes actively warring with each other for control over Caerns and kinfolk communities was a thing. When the Tribes weren't widely distributed and very few Septs had more than one Tribe in them; so the idea that women could just go join the Black Furies wasn't really an option for most Garou to consider.</div> </div> </div> </div>What time frame are we talkin about. 1000years back, or 10.000 years.<br /> In any case, sure the tribes were in conflict with each other, and probably the Black Furies lost territory to other tribes, but might just as well regained some. Possibly now defunct SIlver Fang houses from Rome conquered their lands. As for the Get of Fenris, there is Shadowlord and Tzimisce territory between them and the Black Furies, so sure they might have had skirmishes and conflict, but no danger of actually being destroyed by the other tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-15T01:13:16-08:00","id":1435525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1435462#post1435462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me at least, doesn't matter if WW decide to include or exclude trans-men, we need something that utterly internalizes this decision as an eternal aspect of the setting, and not something that's obviously a writer telling us all to interpret something this way.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Let's move on from this topic, shall we.</b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-15T07:37:00-08:00","id":1435556,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, is there any stuff in Changing Ways that people actually like and want to use in their games?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-15T09:42:34-08:00","id":1435564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1435556#post1435556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, is there any stuff in Changing Ways that people actually like and want to use in their games?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that bad. Though a lot of the ok stuff is -stating the obvious/what I was doing anyway-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-15T12:38:14-08:00","id":1435579,"title":"","content":"The mechanics of the book are actually pretty good. Chapter 5's discussion of Gifts and Rites and how to toy with them a bit is also nice (esp, if you want to let players actually try to invent their own), and the Gifts and Rites presented are all ones most STs shouldn't have a reason to object to in general; like many, some are niche enough you might not want them in a specific game of course or can be way too good/bad depending on play style. Black Mamba Strike being a Rank 4 Gift is either on point for being awesome, or worthless, depending on how you tend to run combat regarding distance between opponents.<br /> <br /> There's a bunch of mechanics that are interesting, even if best taken as optional rules instead of default ones. Healing Dysfunction as an option for botching a roll to heal in combat, is a nice touch at giving Garou more of a feeling of being living creatures with bodies that don't always do what they want (and makes Battle Scars a bit less of a hand-wave).<br /> <br /> Treating the pack as a character with its own stats has a lot of merit to it, esp. if you have larger packs with NPCs and PCs in them. The new Pack Tactics rules are a good addition, but aren't well integrated with the ones in the core book to the point where they're basically two parallel but different things.<br /> <br /> The Metis Deformities are very hit or miss though.<br /> <br /> A lot of the actual writing in the book is OK. It's a book mostly about role-playing advice, but there isn't really much in the way of new insight and a lot of the suggestions are hit or miss with any given group. It's one of the reasons why the really bad stuff (and even the not so bad but still weird stuff like the new terms) dominates discussion of the book... the majority of it is just OK and a lot of people aren't going to find it worth the cost to read things they already know with different phrasing. There's a few, but not nearly enough, points in the book that actually spark some interesting ideas about ways to play the game you might not have considered before (I'd say the best ones are in the pack and Gift/Rite chapters).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-17T06:52:07-08:00","id":1435742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1427414-so-changing-ways?p=1435556#post1435556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, is there any stuff in Changing Ways that people actually like and want to use in their games?</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly liked it, the only thing I would argue, is that when books talk about auspices, they repeat the same stuff, same archetypes every time.<br /> I would like to see more various ways to uphold the roles of the auspices, more creative and out of stereotype ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}